":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cf9abTLxsgEqSCnxPbfX2\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01WaiyZXo1dB23jpSnXJ1173\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":495,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":33446,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":495},\"output_tokens\":20,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d\",\"uuid\":\"e8f0e489-1f1e-40c7-965b-afaac7fc7b1f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-17T19:40:44.628Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cf9abStBZX3Fd5S82iipi\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01WaiyZXo1dB23jpSnXJ1173\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo\"}}}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WaiyZXo1dB23jpSnXJ1173\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n2\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"attavo: the command.\\n3\\t\\n4\\t    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\\n5\\t    attavo spec-gate [N]\\n6\\t    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\\n7\\t    attavo approval-status [N]\\n8\\t    attavo build [N]\\n9\\t    attavo verify [N]\\n10\\t    attavo file-findings [N]\\n11\\t    attavo file-stops [N]\\n12\\t    attavo counsel [N]\\n13\\t    attavo record-only\\n14\\t    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\\n15\\t    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready]\\n16\\t    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\\n17\\t    attavo stops [N] [--json]\\n18\\t\\n19\\tThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts four proofs against a\\n20\\ttenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\\n21\\t\\n22\\t  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\\n23\\t                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\\n24\\t                             and carries a non-empty retires\\n25\\t  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\\n26\\t                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\\n27\\t                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\\n28\\t                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\\n29\\t  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\\n30\\t                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\\n31\\t                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\\n32\\t                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\\n33\\t                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\\n34\\t                             carries its own record paths this way)\\n35\\t  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\\n36\\t                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\\n37\\t                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\\n38\\t                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\\n39\\t                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\\n40\\t                             heading when a build failed after running\\n41\\t                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\\n42\\t                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\\n43\\t                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\\n44\\t                             never refused\\n45\\t\\n46\\tNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\\n47\\tblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\\n48\\tis done.\\n49\\t\\n50\\tspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\\n51\\tfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\\n52\\tis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\\n53\\tbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\\n54\\trejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\\n55\\teven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\\n56\\tbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\\n57\\tfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\\n58\\tthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\\n59\\tone enforces.\\n60\\t\\n61\\tbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\\n62\\tdeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\\n63\\tapproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\\n64\\t(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\\n65\\tGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\\n66\\tconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\\n67\\tspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\\n68\\tbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\\n69\\tevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\\n70\\tdeclared \\\"reports\\\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\\n71\\tit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\\n72\\tnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\\n73\\tsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\\n74\\ttests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\\n75\\twhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\\n76\\twhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\\n77\\tthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\\n78\\tnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\\n79\\tbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\\n80\\trefused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\\n81\\tthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\\n82\\texits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\\n83\\tunder an \\\"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\\\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\\n84\\tit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\\n85\\t{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\\n86\\talready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\\n87\\tbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\\n88\\tenforces.\\n89\\t\\n90\\tverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\\n91\\tstatus pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\\n92\\ta tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\\n93\\tline per check as \\\"<name> <conclusion>\\\". verify runs it on the build\\n94\\trecord's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\\n95\\tskipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\\n96\\tadapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\\n97\\tcalled red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\\n98\\t[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\\n99\\tthe build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\\n100\\tfindings and its declared \\\"reports\\\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\\n101\\tbuild or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\\n102\\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\\n103\\tresult. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\\n104\\tcarries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\\n105\\tcarries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\\n106\\tthe item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\\n107\\trefuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\\n108\\tretires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\\n109\\tfull rules both enforce.\\n110\\t\\n111\\tfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\\n112\\tissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\\n113\\tclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\\n114\\tlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\\n115\\tbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\\n116\\tfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\\n117\\tthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\\n118\\tcommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\\n119\\tnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\\n120\\tempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\\n121\\tcould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\\n122\\t\\n123\\tcounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\\n124\\twhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\\n125\\tpoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\\n126\\tapproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\\n127\\t[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\\n128\\tread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\\n129\\tclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\\n130\\titem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\\n131\\troot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\\n132\\tsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\\n133\\tstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\\n134\\tcitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\\n135\\tdiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\\n136\\t(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\\n137\\tand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\\n138\\tthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\\n139\\ttranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\\n140\\tcaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\\n141\\twritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\\n142\\trecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\\n143\\tenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\\n144\\t\\n145\\trecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\\n146\\tpaths.records; 1 otherwise; 2 with no manifest. Core logic about a git\\n147\\tcheckout, not a forge's shell -- a workflow template's push-and-retrigger\\n148\\tguard is one line reading this exit code instead of carrying its own\\n149\\tcopy of the check.\\n150\\t\\n151\\tattest refuses (exit 1) unless the latest spec, approval, build, and\\n152\\tverify records for an item all exist and chain: the build's approval_sha\\n153\\tnames the latest approval, and the verify's build_sha names that build --\\n154\\ta re-approval after a build must force a re-run of what changed. With no\\n155\\tN given it derives the item from the record paths HEAD's merge commit\\n156\\ttouched under paths.records/<N>/, not from a branch name, which a squash\\n157\\tmerge discards and which names a forge's convention the product does not\\n158\\tknow; more than one item derived is a refusal naming what it found. Zero\\n159\\tis not a defect -- not every merge is an item merge -- exit 0, nothing\\n160\\tprinted but a line saying so.\\n161\\t\\n162\\tattest never writes. On a coherent chain it prints the attestation\\n163\\tstatement -- validating against schema/attestation.schema.json -- to\\n164\\tstdout as JSON and exits 0: the item, its four records and their shas,\\n165\\tand the commit the statement was computed at (sha and merge_sha are the\\n166\\tsame commit here; on the merge group that commit is the one that lands).\\n167\\tThe four stage records already under paths.records are the evidence for\\n168\\tthat statement; a forge-specific template signs the printed JSON,\\n169\\tunmodified, as the predicate, against the commit that lands, on the merge\\n170\\tgroup -- and the signed bundle in the forge's attestation store is the\\n171\\tseal over it. attest itself never signs anything and never talks to a\\n172\\tsigning service. --partial (issue #67) is for a pull request, where the\\n173\\trecord a complete chain would need is the output of a later stage that is\\n174\\titself waiting on this check: a missing later record is \\\"not yet\\\" (exit\\n175\\t0, naming the item and the stages present and absent, no statement\\n176\\tprinted) rather than a refusal, while the two chain assertions -- build's\\n177\\tapproval_sha names the latest approval, verify's build_sha names the\\n178\\tlatest build -- still run over whatever records exist. merge_group and a\\n179\\tpush to main still demand the whole chain. See issue #69's lane for the\\n180\\tfull rules it enforces.\\n181\\t\\n182\\tdrive reads an item's latest records and a forge's own check conclusions\\n183\\tand performs the next mechanical step, and only that step, then stops: no\\n184\\tvalid approval refuses by name and runs nothing; no passing build bound to\\n185\\tthat approval runs build; a passing build with the forge green on the\\n186\\tbranch head (polled for a bound, not the manifest) runs verify; a passing\\n187\\tverify with the forge still green prints that the item is ready to merge\\n188\\tand stops there -- the merge is never drive's own act, and it enqueues\\n189\\tnothing. A record build or verify writes that is not pass is counseled (counsel,\\n190\\tissue #100) and filed (file-stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\\n191\\tso its .filed marker exists in time to be committed alongside it; drive\\n192\\tthen commits the stage record and the counsel record together -- each\\n193\\twith its own log and marker -- with `git commit --only`, never sweeping\\n194\\tthe index, and pushes; a push a divergent remote rejects\\n195\\tis retried once after `git pull --no-rebase --no-edit`, never a rebase,\\n196\\tsince the record already names the commit's sha. drive writes no record\\n197\\tof its own: a second run in the same state repeats the same step or the\\n198\\tsame stop, reading exactly what the prior run left behind -- the marker\\n199\\tincluded, so a stop already filed is never filed again, from this\\n200\\tworktree or a fresh one. See issue #84's lane for the full rules it\\n201\\tenforces.\\n202\\t\\n203\\t--until-ready (issue #100's own followups) repeats step-and-wait --\\n204\\tstep, the forge poll already inside a step, step again -- in the same\\n205\\tprocess, rather than making the caller invoke drive again after every\\n206\\tpassing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\\n207\\town account (a refusal, a halted or failed or refused record, or the\\n208\\tforge never going green); a step that stops still prints exactly what\\n209\\tthe same step would print without the flag. Without --until-ready,\\n210\\tdrive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\\n211\\t\\n212\\tledger reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\\n213\\tpaths.records when N is omitted), it walks the commits from the item's\\n214\\tfirst spec commit to its merge (the same derivation doctor's proof two\\n215\\tand attest use) or to HEAD when the item has not merged, and prints one\\n216\\trow per act: the sha, the identity as git names it, and a class from a\\n217\\tclosed list -- spec, amend, approve, launch, record, change, transport,\\n218\\tmerge -- derived from who committed it and, for an approval, build, or\\n219\\tverify record, what the record itself says. A summary line follows:\\n220\\toperator acts (approve, amend, launch, transport, merge), product acts\\n221\\t(record), executor commits (change), stops (non-pass records), and\\n222\\tsince (the product version on the first record). A build or verify\\n223\\trecord's own commit, from before v0.18.0 gave the driver and the\\n224\\texecutor their own identities, prints as record-or-launch with a note,\\n225\\tcounted toward neither total, rather than guessed. --json prints the\\n226\\trows and the summary as one object. See issue #128's lane for the full\\n227\\trules it enforces.\\n228\\t\\n229\\tstops reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\\n230\\tpaths.records when N is omitted), one row per non-pass build or verify\\n231\\trecord: the record, its stop's class, provenance, and detail, and the\\n232\\tanswerer -- \\\"counsel:<verdict>\\\" when a counsel record read this exact\\n233\\tstop, else \\\"person\\\" for a question, else \\\"guard\\\" for a class a guard\\n234\\talone raised (GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES), else \\\"none\\\". A record too old to\\n235\\tcarry stop at all prints the doctor's own phrase for it, \\\"before stop\\n236\\twas recorded\\\", and is counted there rather than by class. Totals per\\n237\\tclass (read from the build record schema's own enum, never retyped) and\\n238\\tper answerer, plus the before-stop count, follow the rows. --json prints\\n239\\tthe rows and the totals as one object. See issue #129's lane for the\\n240\\tfull rules it enforces.\\n241\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n242\\tfrom __future__ import annotations\\n243\\t\\n244\\timport fnmatch\\n245\\timport json\\n246\\timport os\\n247\\timport re\\n248\\timport shlex\\n249\\timport shutil\\n250\\timport subprocess\\n251\\timport sys\\n252\\timport tempfile\\n253\\timport time\\n254\\timport tomllib\\n255\\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\n256\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\n257\\t\\n258\\tMANIFEST = \\\"attavo.toml\\\"\\n259\\tSTAGES = (\\\"spec\\\", \\\"approval\\\", \\\"build\\\", \\\"verify\\\")\\n260\\tCRITERION_TIMEOUT = 120\\n261\\tRECORD_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^([a-z]+)-([0-9]{2,})\\\\.json$\\\")\\n262\\tBUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET = 3\\n263\\tBUILD_HALT_EXIT = 3\\n264\\tCHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES = 200\\n265\\tPRODUCT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\\n266\\t# issue #84: a constant the lane names, not a manifest key, until a tenant\\n267\\t# disagrees -- how long drive gives a forge's checks room to conclude\\n268\\t# before it gives up and stops rather than call a judge on a tree the\\n269\\t# forge has not yet finished reading. Tenant zero's own checks conclude\\n270\\t# about five minutes after a push; the default bound gives them room to\\n271\\t# finish so a person is not the one re-running drive after CI, which is\\n272\\t# exactly the transport act this lane retires. ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\\n273\\t# and ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S, read at call time rather than once at\\n274\\t# import, are for a test's own clock, not a tenant's -- there is no\\n275\\t# manifest key for either.\\n276\\tDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S = 600.0\\n277\\tDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S = 20.0\\n278\\t\\n279\\t\\n280\\tdef drive_forge_poll_bound_s() -> float:\\n281\\t    return float(os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\\\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S))\\n282\\t\\n283\\t\\n284\\tdef drive_forge_poll_interval_s() -> float:\\n285\\t    return float(os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\\\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S))\\n286\\t\\n287\\t\\n288\\tclass Proof:\\n289\\t    def __init__(self, key: str, title: str) -> None:\\n290\\t        self.key = key\\n291\\t        self.title = title\\n292\\t        self.holds = False\\n293\\t        self.reason = \\\"\\\"\\n294\\t        self.extra: dict = {}\\n295\\t\\n296\\t    def fail(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \\\"Proof\\\":\\n297\\t        self.holds, self.reason = False, reason\\n298\\t        self.extra.update(extra)\\n299\\t        return self\\n300\\t\\n301\\t    def hold(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \\\"Proof\\\":\\n302\\t        self.holds, self.reason = True, reason\\n303\\t        self.extra.update(extra)\\n304\\t        return self\\n305\\t\\n306\\t    def as_dict(self) -> dict:\\n307\\t        return {\\\"proof\\\": self.key, \\\"title\\\": self.title,\\n308\\t                \\\"holds\\\": self.holds, \\\"reason\\\": self.reason, **self.extra}\\n309\\t\\n310\\t\\n311\\tdef read_manifest(root: Path) -> dict | None:\\n312\\t    path = root / MANIFEST\\n313\\t    if not path.is_file():\\n314\\t        return None\\n315\\t    with path.open(\\\"rb\\\") as fh:\\n316\\t        return tomllib.load(fh)\\n317\\t\\n318\\t\\n319\\tdef git(root: Path, *args: str, env: dict | None = None) -> str:\\n320\\t    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), *args],\\n321\\t                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\\n322\\t    if out.returncode != 0:\\n323\\t        raise RuntimeError(out.stderr.strip() or \\\"git failed\\\")\\n324\\t    return out.stdout\\n325\\t\\n326\\t\\n327\\tdef product_version() -> str:\\n328\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"What the running program is. Three fallbacks, in order, and never an\\n329\\t    exception -- this runs inside write_record, after the work it\\n330\\t    describes already happened, and a raise here would lose the record\\n331\\t    for an invocation that already ran:\\n332\\t\\n333\\t      1. ATTAVO_PRODUCT_VERSION, when the environment sets it. The forge\\n334\\t         action sets this from its own ref (action.yml, not here -- this\\n335\\t         function stays forge-agnostic).\\n336\\t      2. git describe --tags --always --dirty against PRODUCT_ROOT: a\\n337\\t         tagged release reports its tag, a checkout reports its commit,\\n338\\t         a dirty tree says so.\\n339\\t      3. \\\"unknown\\\", when PRODUCT_ROOT is not a git repository at all --\\n340\\t         the case for a forge that extracts this action from a tarball\\n341\\t         rather than a git checkout, which is exactly when (1) is\\n342\\t         expected to already have supplied the answer.\\n343\\t\\n344\\t    Distinct from the tenant's product_pin -- an operator running a\\n345\\t    checkout, which is how every build and verify have actually been run\\n346\\t    so far, bypasses the pin entirely (issue #49).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n347\\t    env = os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_PRODUCT_VERSION\\\")\\n348\\t    if env:\\n349\\t        return env\\n350\\t    try:\\n351\\t        return git(PRODUCT_ROOT, \\\"describe\\\", \\\"--tags\\\", \\\"--always\\\", \\\"--dirty\\\").strip()\\n352\\t    except RuntimeError:\\n353\\t        return \\\"unknown\\\"\\n354\\t\\n355\\t\\n356\\tdef now_iso() -> str:\\n357\\t    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\\\")\\n358\\t\\n359\\t\\n360\\tdef derive_item_id(root: Path) -> str | None:\\n361\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"ATTAVO_ITEM first, not last: a rejection fixture's own item id must\\n362\\t    win over whatever attavo/N-* branch the enclosing tenant repository\\n363\\t    happens to be checked out on -- the common case is doctor running from\\n364\\t    a real item's own branch, where a fallback-only env var would never be\\n365\\t    consulted at all and every gate fixture would silently resolve to the\\n366\\t    real item instead of its own.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n367\\t    env_item = os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_ITEM\\\")\\n368\\t    if env_item:\\n369\\t        return env_item\\n370\\t    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--abbrev-ref\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\"],\\n371\\t                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n372\\t    branch = out.stdout.strip()\\n373\\t    m = re.match(r\\\"^attavo/(\\\\d+)-\\\", branch)\\n374\\t    return m.group(1) if m else None\\n375\\t\\n376\\t\\n377\\tdef fixture_item_id(fixture: Path) -> str | None:\\n378\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one item id under a rejection fixture's own paths.specs, so the\\n379\\t    doctor can export it as ATTAVO_ITEM: a fixture carries no attavo/N-*\\n380\\t    branch for a gate command with no argument to derive from otherwise.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n381\\t    fm = read_manifest(fixture)\\n382\\t    specs_rel = ((fm or {}).get(\\\"paths\\\") or {}).get(\\\"specs\\\")\\n383\\t    if not specs_rel:\\n384\\t        return None\\n385\\t    specs_dir = fixture / specs_rel\\n386\\t    if not specs_dir.is_dir():\\n387\\t        return None\\n388\\t    items = sorted(p.name for p in specs_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir())\\n389\\t    return items[0] if len(items) == 1 else None\\n390\\t\\n391\\t\\n392\\tclass ShallowCheckoutError(RuntimeError):\\n393\\t    pass\\n394\\t\\n395\\t\\n396\\tdef last_commit_touching(root: Path, relpath: str) -> str | None:\\n397\\t    shallow = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--is-shallow-repository\\\"],\\n398\\t                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n399\\t    if shallow.stdout.strip() == \\\"true\\\":\\n400\\t        raise ShallowCheckoutError(\\n401\\t            \\\"shallow checkout: git log -1 -- <path> returns HEAD for every path on a \\\"\\n402\\t            \\\"shallow clone; check out with fetch-depth: 0\\\")\\n403\\t    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"log\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\", \\\"--\\\", relpath],\\n404\\t                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n405\\t    sha = out.stdout.strip()\\n406\\t    return sha or None\\n407\\t\\n408\\t\\n409\\t# --- record files: <stage>-NN.json, one per attempt, never overwritten ---\\n410\\t\\n411\\tSCHEMA_RECORDS_DIR = PRODUCT_ROOT / \\\"schema\\\" / \\\"records\\\"\\n412\\t\\n413\\t\\n414\\tdef stage_schema(stage: str) -> dict:\\n415\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"schema/records/<stage>.schema.json -- this repository's own\\n416\\t    declaration of that stage's record shape (issue #60). The only\\n417\\t    artifact the outbound contract needs; there is no accessor for it\\n418\\t    beyond reading the file.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n419\\t    return json.loads((SCHEMA_RECORDS_DIR / f\\\"{stage}.schema.json\\\").read_text())\\n420\\t\\n421\\t\\n422\\tdef schema_id_version(schema: dict) -> int:\\n423\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The trailing integer of a schema's $id (\\\".../records/build/2\\\" -> 2)\\n424\\t    -- the single place a record shape's version lives. write_record reads\\n425\\t    this at call time rather than carrying its own copy, so the version it\\n426\\t    stamps cannot drift from what the schema declares (issue #60).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n427\\t    return int(schema[\\\"$id\\\"].rsplit(\\\"/\\\", 1)[-1])\\n428\\t\\n429\\t\\n430\\tclass RecordItemMismatch(RuntimeError):\\n431\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A record's item field disagrees with the directory it was read\\n432\\t    from (issue #60, acceptance 5) -- a misfiled or copied record, refused\\n433\\t    rather than trusted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n434\\t\\n435\\t\\n436\\tdef _load_record(path: Path, item_id: str) -> dict:\\n437\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one place in this repository that turns a record file's bytes\\n438\\t    into a dict (issue #60, acceptance 6). Defaults record_version to 1\\n439\\t    when absent -- version 1 is every record written before this release\\n440\\t    and is never migrated -- and fills item from the directory when\\n441\\t    absent; refuses when a present item disagrees with it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n442\\t    data = json.loads(path.read_text())\\n443\\t    data.setdefault(\\\"record_version\\\", 1)\\n444\\t    item = data.get(\\\"item\\\")\\n445\\t    if item is None:\\n446\\t        data[\\\"item\\\"] = item_id\\n447\\t    elif item != item_id:\\n448\\t        raise RecordItemMismatch(\\n449\\t            f\\\"{path}: item {item!r} disagrees with its directory {item_id!r}\\\")\\n450\\t    return data\\n451\\t\\n452\\t\\n453\\tdef parse_attempts(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> dict[int, dict]:\\n454\\t    attempts: dict[int, dict] = {}\\n455\\t    if not records_dir.is_dir():\\n456\\t        return attempts\\n457\\t    for f in records_dir.glob(f\\\"{stage}-*.json\\\"):\\n458\\t        m = RECORD_RE.match(f.name)\\n459\\t        if not m or m.group(1) != stage:\\n460\\t            continue\\n461\\t        try:\\n462\\t            attempts[int(m.group(2))] = _load_record(f, records_dir.name)\\n463\\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n464\\t            continue\\n465\\t    return attempts\\n466\\t\\n467\\t\\n468\\tdef latest_record(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> dict | None:\\n469\\t    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\\n470\\t    return attempts[max(attempts)] if attempts else None\\n471\\t\\n472\\t\\n473\\tdef next_attempt_number(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> int:\\n474\\t    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\\n475\\t    return (max(attempts) + 1) if attempts else 1\\n476\\t\\n477\\t\\n478\\tdef latest_attempt_path(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> Path | None:\\n479\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The path of the highest-numbered <stage>-NN.json, or None.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n480\\t    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\\n481\\t    if not attempts:\\n482\\t        return None\\n483\\t    return records_dir / f\\\"{stage}-{max(attempts):02d}.json\\\"\\n484\\t\\n485\\t\\n486\\tdef write_record(records_dir: Path, stage: str, record: dict, m: dict, item: str,\\n487\\t                 log: str | None = None) -> Path:\\n488\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every record gains record_version (this stage schema's own $id\\n489\\t    version -- issue #60) and item (verbatim from the caller, matching the\\n490\\t    record's directory segment), plus product_version (what ran, derived\\n491\\t    here) and product_pin (what the tenant declared, copied verbatim from\\n492\\t    the manifest, or null when the manifest carries no [attavo] table) --\\n493\\t    the latter two recorded, never enforced (issue #49). A manifest\\n494\\t    missing the table is an absent fact, not a crash: this is the one\\n495\\t    caller of write_record that must not raise on a shape the manifest\\n496\\t    schema forbids but tomllib.load happily returns.\\n497\\t\\n498\\t    Refuses (raises ValueError) a record carrying a key this stage's\\n499\\t    schema does not declare -- the declared key set enforced with the\\n500\\t    standard library, not a jsonschema import: bin/attavo is a single\\n501\\t    script a tenant pins, and a runtime dependency changes installation.\\n502\\t\\n503\\t    Also refuses a `status: \\\"failed\\\"` record that carries no trail at all\\n504\\t    -- log the empty or missing text it will sit beside, and refusal and\\n505\\t    halted (where the stage's schema has them) both null (issue #53).\\n506\\t    `returned`, `pass`, `halted`, and `refused` owe no such trail. log is\\n507\\t    None for a stage that invoked no adapter (verify's `returned`), which\\n508\\t    write_record then writes no log file for; otherwise the log is\\n509\\t    written before the record, so a refusal leaves no half-pair.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n510\\t    records_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n511\\t    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\\n512\\t    schema = stage_schema(stage)\\n513\\t    record = {**record, \\\"record_version\\\": schema_id_version(schema), \\\"item\\\": item,\\n514\\t              \\\"product_version\\\": product_version(),\\n515\\t              \\\"product_pin\\\": (m.get(\\\"attavo\\\") or {}).get(\\\"version\\\")}\\n516\\t    undeclared = set(record) - set(schema.get(\\\"properties\\\", {}))\\n517\\t    if undeclared:\\n518\\t        raise ValueError(f\\\"write_record: {stage} record carries key(s) its schema does not \\\"\\n519\\t                         f\\\"declare: {', '.join(sorted(undeclared))}\\\")\\n520\\t    if (record.get(\\\"status\\\") == \\\"failed\\\" and not log\\n521\\t            and record.get(\\\"refusal\\\") is None and record.get(\\\"halted\\\") is None):\\n522\\t        raise ValueError(f\\\"write_record: {stage} record status is 'failed' with no log, \\\"\\n523\\t                         f\\\"refusal, or halted to say why\\\")\\n524\\t    path = records_dir / f\\\"{stage}-{nn:02d}.json\\\"\\n525\\t    if log is not None:\\n526\\t        path.with_suffix(\\\".log\\\").write_text(log)\\n527\\t    path.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n528\\t    return path\\n529\\t\\n530\\t\\n531\\t# --- stop: every non-pass build or verify record's class and cause (issue\\n532\\t# #89) -- derived here, at write time, from the refusal, halted, and log\\n533\\t# the caller already has. Never a fresh read of anything: the tenant zero\\n534\\t# specimens this retires (#576 build-11, #659 build-01 and verify-01) are\\n535\\t# exactly a stop the product wrote with nothing beside it to explain\\n536\\t# itself after the fact. ---\\n537\\t\\n538\\tSTOP_CLASSES = (\\\"non-question\\\", \\\"outlived-invocation\\\", \\\"no-cause\\\", \\\"forge-unconcluded\\\",\\n539\\t               \\\"ceiling\\\", \\\"claims-boundary\\\", \\\"repeated-act\\\", \\\"unclassed\\\", \\\"question\\\",\\n540\\t               \\\"environment\\\", \\\"gate\\\")\\n541\\tSTOP_PROVENANCES = (\\\"product\\\", \\\"tenant\\\", \\\"executor\\\", \\\"spec\\\")\\n542\\t\\n543\\t# Beyond the enum spelling itself, the prose issue #88 actually shipped\\n544\\t# (adapters/claude-code/run and adapters/codex/run, on main since\\n545\\t# v0.16.0) once put a class's own name, or a real specimen's wording of\\n546\\t# it, in the transcript for the generic match below to find. Issue #94\\n547\\t# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\\n548\\t# (below): non-question's own halt line (\\\"halted: class non-question\\\")\\n549\\t# would otherwise still satisfy the bare-name match here with no adapter\\n550\\t# report-line field involved at all, and outlived-invocation's refusal\\n551\\t# never named its class in text to begin with, so both are disabled here\\n552\\t# -- the same pattern issue #93 established for ceiling, just below,\\n553\\t# rather than removed outright.\\n554\\tCLASS_TEXT_MARKERS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\\n555\\t    \\\"non-question\\\": (),\\n556\\t    \\\"outlived-invocation\\\": (),\\n557\\t    # Issue #93: ceiling's own text-based check is CEILING_MARKERS, below,\\n558\\t    # with provenance \\\"product\\\" -- a fact about the tool, not an executor\\n559\\t    # judgment like non-question/outlived-invocation are. Left at the\\n560\\t    # default (the class's own name, \\\"ceiling\\\"), the generic match above\\n561\\t    # would instead catch adapters/codex/run's and\\n562\\t    # adapters/claude-code/run's own pre-emptive refusal -- which must\\n563\\t    # carry the word \\\"ceiling\\\" by the same issue's own brief -- as\\n564\\t    # provenance \\\"executor\\\", before CEILING_MARKERS is ever consulted.\\n565\\t    \\\"ceiling\\\": (),\\n566\\t    # A genuine question (issue #100's own followups) is read structurally\\n567\\t    # -- status \\\"halted\\\" carrying a non-empty halted.question -- not by\\n568\\t    # scanning for the literal word \\\"question\\\", which the question's own\\n569\\t    # text very often contains regardless of what it is actually asking.\\n570\\t    # Left at the default, the generic match above would misclassify any\\n571\\t    # question that happens to use the word \\\"question\\\" as executor\\n572\\t    # provenance, before the structural check in derive_stop is reached.\\n573\\t    \\\"question\\\": (),\\n574\\t    # environment/tenant (issue #115) is set directly by cmd_build's own\\n575\\t    # preflight -- the one caller who knows a [checks].command exited 2\\n576\\t    # on the approved tree -- never derived from adapter text. Left at\\n577\\t    # the default, the generic match above would catch the word\\n578\\t    # \\\"environment\\\" anywhere in a log or refusal (e.g. codex's own\\n579\\t    # OPENAI_API_KEY auth-mismatch refusal, adapters/codex/run's\\n580\\t    # check_auth) as an environment/executor stop that never happened.\\n581\\t    \\\"environment\\\": (),\\n582\\t}\\n583\\t\\n584\\t# Known tool error text for a declared ceiling -- issue #86's own specimen\\n585\\t# (codex's \\\"Input exceeds...\\\" line on a diff too large to judge) is\\n586\\t# \\\"input_too_large\\\"; a matching line anywhere in the log, not only its\\n587\\t# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \\\"[adapter exited\\n588\\t# N]\\\" after whatever the tool itself printed. \\\"ceiling exceeded\\\" is issue\\n589\\t# #93's own addition: both adapters now refuse pre-emptively, before the\\n590\\t# tool is ever invoked, against a declared or fixed input limit, and\\n591\\t# their refusal text is not caught by any of the three markers above.\\n592\\tCEILING_MARKERS = (\\\"input_too_large\\\", \\\"exceeds the maximum context length\\\",\\n593\\t                  \\\"context_length_exceeded\\\", \\\"ceiling exceeded\\\")\\n594\\t\\n595\\t\\n596\\t# Issue #100's followups: an unclassed detail is the log's last line\\n597\\t# verbatim, and that line is sometimes an adapter's own event JSON or a\\n598\\t# tool's full error text -- thousands of characters wide. Capped here,\\n599\\t# at write time, so a filed issue's own summary of it (file-stops'\\n600\\t# log_tail already carries the full picture) stays short; the class\\n601\\t# itself, \\\"unclassed\\\", already says the full explanation lives in the\\n602\\t# log, not in this field.\\n603\\tUNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS = 200\\n604\\t\\n605\\t\\n606\\tdef _log_last_line(log: str | None) -> str:\\n607\\t    lines = [l for l in (log or \\\"\\\").splitlines() if l.strip()]\\n608\\t    last = lines[-1] if lines else \\\"\\\"\\n609\\t    return last[:UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS]\\n610\\t\\n611\\t\\n612\\tdef _carries_a_known_class(text: str | None) -> str | None:\\n613\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whichever of STOP_CLASSES this text names -- its own spelling, or\\n614\\t    one of CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS' real-world phrasings of it, when that\\n615\\t    class is not disabled there -- or None. Issue #88 is where an\\n616\\t    adapter's own halt or refusal first named its class this way; issue\\n617\\t    #93 added ceiling's own pre-emptive refusal to that set and disabled\\n618\\t    its bare-name match (CEILING_MARKERS covers it instead); issue #94\\n619\\t    disables non-question and outlived-invocation the same way, reading\\n620\\t    both from the adapter's own report line (derive_stop's report_class)\\n621\\t    now instead.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n622\\t    text = text or \\\"\\\"\\n623\\t    for name in STOP_CLASSES:\\n624\\t        markers = CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS.get(name, (name,))\\n625\\t        if any(marker in text for marker in markers):\\n626\\t            return name\\n627\\t    return None\\n628\\t\\n629\\t\\n630\\tdef derive_stop(status: str, *, refusal: str | None = None, halted: dict | None = None,\\n631\\t                log: str | None = None, report_class: str | None = None,\\n632\\t                refusal_provenance: str | None = None) -> dict | None:\\n633\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The stop field for a build or verify record: None for status \\\"pass\\\",\\n634\\t    else {class, provenance, detail} from what the caller already knows.\\n635\\t\\n636\\t      - report_class -- payload.get(\\\"class\\\") off the adapter's own report\\n637\\t        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\\n638\\t        that class, provenance \\\"executor\\\". build.schema.json and\\n639\\t        verify.schema.json stay untouched by issue #88 on purpose, so the\\n640\\t        class lives only on the report line, never a structured field\\n641\\t        cmd_build or cmd_verify forwards on its own account; the caller\\n642\\t        reads payload itself and passes this in, since only it still has\\n643\\t        payload once an iteration ends. This is non-question's and\\n644\\t        outlived-invocation's only path to a record now (issue #94):\\n645\\t        CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS disables both for the text scan below, the\\n646\\t        same way issue #93 disabled ceiling's bare-name match there. A\\n647\\t        class an adapter does not yet put on its report line --\\n648\\t        outlived-invocation today, since that refusal path prints no\\n649\\t        report line at all -- falls to unclassed below, same as any\\n650\\t        other unnamed cause, until the adapter that raises it puts a\\n651\\t        class on the line the way non-question already does.\\n652\\t      - a halt carrying a non-empty halted.question, once it is not a\\n653\\t        non-question caught above, is a genuine question -- question/spec,\\n654\\t        with the question's own first line as detail (issue #100's\\n655\\t        followups). This is the specimen issue #100 itself was built to\\n656\\t        retire: tenant zero's #663 build-01, a proper question, classed\\n657\\t        unclassed/product and filed as a product defect with the wrong\\n658\\t        provenance -- a question is about the definition of done, which is\\n659\\t        a person's or a ruling's to answer, never the product's own\\n660\\t        mechanism.\\n661\\t      - failing that, a refusal or the log itself that already names its\\n662\\t        class in text (issue #88, #93 for ceiling's own pre-emptive\\n663\\t        refusal) is that class, provenance \\\"executor\\\" -- the log is\\n664\\t        checked because neither adapter's refusal *field* carries the\\n665\\t        class today; the class-naming line each adapter prints reaches\\n666\\t        only the transcript\\n667\\t      - a refusal that is not that -- the write-outside-claims path\\n668\\t        itself, not the \\\"commit ... not authored by the executor\\\" shape\\n669\\t        -- is claims-boundary/spec, unless the caller already knows this\\n670\\t        refusal touched paths.records or paths.specs (issue #140:\\n671\\t        protected_path_touched, checked ahead of the ordinary claims\\n672\\t        match in cmd_build) and passes refusal_provenance=\\\"executor\\\" --\\n673\\t        the product's own directories are not a claim a spec makes, so a\\n674\\t        refusal there is not the spec's boundary to answer for\\n675\\t      - a returned verify (the forge was not green; no adapter ran) is\\n676\\t        forge-unconcluded/tenant\\n677\\t      - an adapter exit whose log carries a declared-ceiling error line is\\n678\\t        ceiling/product\\n679\\t      - anything else is unclassed/product, with the log's last line\\n680\\t        (capped at UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS) as its detail -- the other\\n681\\t        class that carries a detail, since every remaining class's\\n682\\t        evidence already lives in refusal, halted, forge_checks, or the\\n683\\t        log itself.\\n684\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n685\\t    if status == \\\"pass\\\":\\n686\\t        return None\\n687\\t    if status == \\\"returned\\\":\\n688\\t        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"forge-unconcluded\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"tenant\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n689\\t    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\\n690\\t        return {\\\"class\\\": report_class, \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"executor\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n691\\t    question = (halted or {}).get(\\\"question\\\")\\n692\\t    if status == \\\"halted\\\" and question:\\n693\\t        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"question\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"spec\\\",\\n694\\t               \\\"detail\\\": question.splitlines()[0]}\\n695\\t    known = _carries_a_known_class(refusal) or _carries_a_known_class(log)\\n696\\t    if known:\\n697\\t        return {\\\"class\\\": known, \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"executor\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n698\\t    if status == \\\"refused\\\" and refusal is not None and not refusal.startswith(\\\"commit \\\"):\\n699\\t        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"claims-boundary\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": refusal_provenance or \\\"spec\\\",\\n700\\t               \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n701\\t    if log and any(marker in log.lower() for marker in CEILING_MARKERS):\\n702\\t        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"ceiling\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"product\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n703\\t    return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"unclassed\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"product\\\", \\\"detail\\\": _log_last_line(log)}\\n704\\t\\n705\\t\\n706\\tdef gate_stop(refusal: str | None) -> dict:\\n707\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The stop for a refused spec-gate record: class \\\"gate\\\", provenance\\n708\\t    \\\"spec\\\", the refusal string itself as cause (issue #137) -- not\\n709\\t    derive_stop's generic claims-boundary/spec fallback issue #133\\n710\\t    reused, which named a boundary the record never crossed: \\\"criterion\\n711\\t    fails against the tree plus stub: doctor-template-absent.sh\\\" is not\\n712\\t    a write outside claims. cmd_spec_gate is untouched by this lane, so\\n713\\t    a spec record still carries no stop field of its own; this is\\n714\\t    synthesized wherever a refused one is read (item_stops,\\n715\\t    cmd_file_stops, proof_no_stop_lacks_cause), never persisted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n716\\t    return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"gate\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"spec\\\", \\\"detail\\\": refusal}\\n717\\t\\n718\\t\\n719\\tdef load_records(records_dir: Path) -> dict[str, dict[str, dict]]:\\n720\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"{item_id: {stage: latest_record}} for every <records>/<item>/<stage>-NN.json.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n721\\t    items: dict[str, dict[str, dict]] = {}\\n722\\t    if not records_dir.is_dir():\\n723\\t        return items\\n724\\t    for item_dir in sorted(p for p in records_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir()):\\n725\\t        by_stage: dict[str, dict[int, dict]] = {}\\n726\\t        for rec in sorted(item_dir.glob(\\\"*.json\\\")):\\n727\\t            m = RECORD_RE.match(rec.name)\\n728\\t            if not m:\\n729\\t                continue\\n730\\t            stage, n = m.group(1), int(m.group(2))\\n731\\t            try:\\n732\\t                data = _load_record(rec, item_dir.name)\\n733\\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n734\\t                continue\\n735\\t            by_stage.setdefault(stage, {})[n] = data\\n736\\t        items[item_dir.name] = {stage: attempts[max(attempts)] for stage, attempts in by_stage.items()}\\n737\\t    return items\\n738\\t\\n739\\t\\n740\\t# --- doctor's three proofs ---\\n741\\t\\n742\\tdef proof_every_gate_rejects(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n743\\t    p = Proof(\\\"every-gate-rejects\\\", \\\"every gate rejects its fixture\\\")\\n744\\t    if m is None:\\n745\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no gate is registered\\\")\\n746\\t    gates = m.get(\\\"gates\\\") or {}\\n747\\t    if not gates:\\n748\\t        return p.fail(\\\"[gates] is empty; a gate that has rejected nothing does not exist\\\")\\n749\\t    fixtures = root / m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"rejections\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n750\\t    # Proposal, not yet ruled on (issue #54): a gate that retires nothing\\n751\\t    # only adds, so proof one reports it here rather than waiting on the\\n752\\t    # schema alone -- read_manifest never validates against the manifest\\n753\\t    # schema at runtime, so a schema requirement is not an enforced one.\\n754\\t    no_retires = [name for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()) if not gate.get(\\\"retires\\\")]\\n755\\t    missing, accepted = [], []\\n756\\t    for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()):\\n757\\t        fixture = fixtures / name\\n758\\t        if not fixture.is_dir():\\n759\\t            missing.append(name)\\n760\\t            continue\\n761\\t        env = dict(os.environ)\\n762\\t        item = fixture_item_id(fixture)\\n763\\t        if item is not None:\\n764\\t            env[\\\"ATTAVO_ITEM\\\"] = item\\n765\\t        run = subprocess.run(gate[\\\"command\\\"], shell=True, cwd=str(fixture),\\n766\\t                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\\n767\\t        if run.returncode == 0:\\n768\\t            accepted.append(name)\\n769\\t    if missing:\\n770\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"gate(s) with no rejection fixture: {', '.join(missing)}\\\")\\n771\\t    if accepted:\\n772\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"gate(s) that accepted their rejection fixture: {', '.join(accepted)}\\\")\\n773\\t    if no_retires:\\n774\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"gate(s) with no retires: {', '.join(no_retires)}\\\")\\n775\\t    return p.hold(f\\\"{len(gates)} gate(s) rejected their fixture\\\")\\n776\\t\\n777\\t\\n778\\tdef merge_introducing_records(root: Path, records_rel: str, item: str,\\n779\\t                              stages: tuple[str, ...]) -> str | None:\\n780\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The merge commit reachable from HEAD whose first-parent diff\\n781\\t    introduces a record for every one of stages, under\\n782\\t    records_rel/item/ -- the same derivation attest itself uses\\n783\\t    (derive_attest_items), read here so proof two requires an item's\\n784\\t    stage records to have arrived by an actual merge, not merely to sit\\n785\\t    in the tree (issue #69, acceptance row 4).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n786\\t    try:\\n787\\t        merges = git(root, \\\"log\\\", \\\"--merges\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\").split()\\n788\\t    except RuntimeError:\\n789\\t        return None\\n790\\t    prefix = f\\\"{records_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item}/\\\"\\n791\\t    for sha in merges:\\n792\\t        try:\\n793\\t            diff = git(root, \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", f\\\"{sha}^1\\\", sha).splitlines()\\n794\\t        except RuntimeError:\\n795\\t            continue\\n796\\t        found: set[str] = set()\\n797\\t        for p in diff:\\n798\\t            if p.startswith(prefix):\\n799\\t                m = RECORD_RE.match(Path(p).name)\\n800\\t                if m:\\n801\\t                    found.add(m.group(1))\\n802\\t        if all(s in found for s in stages):\\n803\\t            return sha\\n804\\t    return None\\n805\\t\\n806\\t\\n807\\tdef proof_one_item_every_stage(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n808\\t    p = Proof(\\\"one-item-every-stage\\\", \\\"one item has traversed every stage\\\")\\n809\\t    if m is None:\\n810\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\\\")\\n811\\t    records_rel = m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"records\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n812\\t    records_dir = root / records_rel\\n813\\t    items = load_records(records_dir)\\n814\\t    if not items:\\n815\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no work item under {records_dir.relative_to(root)}\\\")\\n816\\t    complete = [item for item, stages in items.items() if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\\n817\\t    if not complete:\\n818\\t        best = max(items.items(), key=lambda kv: len(kv[1]))\\n819\\t        lacking = [s for s in STAGES if s not in best[1]]\\n820\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no item carries every stage; item {best[0]} lacks {', '.join(lacking)}\\\")\\n821\\t\\n822\\t    # issue #74: a complete item is counted only when its chain holds --\\n823\\t    # attavo attest refuses a build re-approved after the fact or a\\n824\\t    # verify whose build went stale, and the coherence gate refuses the\\n825\\t    # merge group on exactly that; a proof that never asked would call a\\n826\\t    # traversal the gate itself would not let through. The refusal text\\n827\\t    # is check_attest_chain's own, never re-typed here.\\n828\\t    refused, held, unmerged = [], [], []\\n829\\t    for item in complete:\\n830\\t        chain, message = check_attest_chain(records_dir / item, item)\\n831\\t        if chain is None:\\n832\\t            refused.append(f\\\"item {item}: {message}\\\")\\n833\\t            continue\\n834\\t        merge_sha = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item, STAGES)\\n835\\t        if merge_sha:\\n836\\t            held.append((item, merge_sha))\\n837\\t        else:\\n838\\t            unmerged.append(item)\\n839\\t\\n840\\t    if held:\\n841\\t        names = \\\", \\\".join(item for item, _ in held)\\n842\\t        shas = \\\", \\\".join(sha[:12] for _, sha in held)\\n843\\t        return p.hold(f\\\"item(s) {names} carry {', '.join(STAGES)} with the chain held, \\\"\\n844\\t                      f\\\"merged at {shas}\\\")\\n845\\t    if refused:\\n846\\t        return p.fail(\\\"; \\\".join(refused))\\n847\\t    return p.fail(f\\\"item(s) {', '.join(unmerged)} carry every stage with the chain held but no \\\"\\n848\\t                  f\\\"merge commit's first-parent diff introduces all of them\\\")\\n849\\t\\n850\\t\\n851\\tdef commit_subject(root: Path, sha: str) -> str:\\n852\\t    return git(root, \\\"log\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--format=%s\\\", sha).strip()\\n853\\t\\n854\\t\\n855\\tdef touches_boundary(root: Path, sha: str, boundary_paths: list[str]) -> bool:\\n856\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whether sha's first-parent diff touches a path [spec.boundary].paths\\n857\\t    declares governed -- an ordinary merge that does is a boundary\\n858\\t    evasion (issue #72): the tenant carried a governed change around the\\n859\\t    path the manifest itself names.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n860\\t    diff = git(root, \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", f\\\"{sha}^1\\\", sha).splitlines()\\n861\\t    return any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, pattern) for path in diff for pattern in boundary_paths)\\n862\\t\\n863\\t\\n864\\tdef proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n865\\t    p = Proof(\\\"no-commit-lacks-record\\\", \\\"no commit lacks a record\\\")\\n866\\t    if m is None:\\n867\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; the tenant has no record boundary\\\")\\n868\\t    try:\\n869\\t        install = git(root, \\\"log\\\", \\\"--diff-filter=A\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\",\\n870\\t                      \\\"--reverse\\\", \\\"--\\\", MANIFEST).split()\\n871\\t    except RuntimeError as exc:\\n872\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"git: {exc}\\\")\\n873\\t    if not install:\\n874\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"{MANIFEST} is not committed; the tenant has no record boundary\\\")\\n875\\t    install_sha = install[0]\\n876\\t    full_chain = git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", f\\\"{install_sha}..HEAD\\\", \\\"--first-parent\\\").split()\\n877\\t    if not full_chain:\\n878\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no commit after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}; nothing has been recorded\\\")\\n879\\t\\n880\\t    # issue #74: [doctor] from lets a tenant declare the doctor's read to\\n881\\t    # start at a later commit on main's first-parent line -- the point\\n882\\t    # after which every push arrived through the queue -- rather than the\\n883\\t    # install commit, which on a repository that adopted the product\\n884\\t    # after its history began is a boundary the doctor cannot otherwise\\n885\\t    # see. Any spelling git resolves is accepted (a short sha, a tag, a\\n886\\t    # ref) -- resolved with rev-parse --verify before the first-parent\\n887\\t    # check runs, so the two failure modes stay distinct: a spelling that\\n888\\t    # names no commit at all, and a commit that names one off the line.\\n889\\t    # Checked, not trusted: neither is silently forgiven back to install.\\n890\\t    declared_from = (m.get(\\\"doctor\\\") or {}).get(\\\"from\\\")\\n891\\t    window_start = install_sha\\n892\\t    if declared_from is not None:\\n893\\t        try:\\n894\\t            resolved_from = git(root, \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", f\\\"{declared_from}^{{commit}}\\\").strip()\\n895\\t        except RuntimeError:\\n896\\t            return p.fail(f\\\"[doctor] from {declared_from} does not resolve to a commit\\\")\\n897\\t        if resolved_from != install_sha and resolved_from not in full_chain:\\n898\\t            return p.fail(f\\\"[doctor] from {declared_from} is not on main's first-parent \\\"\\n899\\t                          f\\\"line after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}\\\")\\n900\\t        window_start = resolved_from\\n901\\t\\n902\\t    if window_start == install_sha:\\n903\\t        window_spec = f\\\"{install_sha}..HEAD\\\"\\n904\\t        commits = full_chain\\n905\\t    else:\\n906\\t        window_spec = f\\\"{window_start}^..HEAD\\\"\\n907\\t        commits = git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", window_spec, \\\"--first-parent\\\").split()\\n908\\t    before_window = len(full_chain) - len(commits)\\n909\\t\\n910\\t    records_rel = m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"records\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n911\\t    records_dir = root / records_rel\\n912\\t    named: set[str] = set()\\n913\\t    for stages in load_records(records_dir).values():\\n914\\t        for rec in stages.values():\\n915\\t            sha = rec.get(\\\"sha\\\")\\n916\\t            if isinstance(sha, str):\\n917\\t                named.add(sha)\\n918\\t            for c in rec.get(\\\"commits\\\", []) or []:\\n919\\t                if isinstance(c, str):\\n920\\t                    named.add(c)\\n921\\t    record_commits = set(git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", window_spec, \\\"--first-parent\\\",\\n922\\t                             \\\"--\\\", records_rel).split()) if records_rel else set()\\n923\\t    merges = set(git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", window_spec, \\\"--first-parent\\\", \\\"--merges\\\").split())\\n924\\t    boundary_paths = ((m.get(\\\"spec\\\") or {}).get(\\\"boundary\\\") or {}).get(\\\"paths\\\") or []\\n925\\t\\n926\\t    # Every first-parent commit in the window is exactly one of three\\n927\\t    # (issue #72): recorded (a record names it, or its diff touches\\n928\\t    # paths.records), ordinary (a merge that doesn't), or unrecorded\\n929\\t    # (anything else -- on a protected main with a queue, a non-merge\\n930\\t    # commit is the only way a change arrives without the forge).\\n931\\t    recorded, ordinary, unrecorded = [], [], []\\n932\\t    ordinary_commits, unrecorded_commits = [], []\\n933\\t    boundary_evasions = 0\\n934\\t    for c in commits:\\n935\\t        if c in named or c in record_commits:\\n936\\t            recorded.append(c)\\n937\\t        elif c in merges:\\n938\\t            ordinary.append(c)\\n939\\t            evasion = bool(boundary_paths and touches_boundary(root, c, boundary_paths))\\n940\\t            if evasion:\\n941\\t                boundary_evasions += 1\\n942\\t            ordinary_commits.append({\\\"sha\\\": c, \\\"subject\\\": commit_subject(root, c),\\n943\\t                                     \\\"boundary_evasion\\\": evasion})\\n944\\t        else:\\n945\\t            unrecorded.append(c)\\n946\\t            unrecorded_commits.append({\\\"sha\\\": c, \\\"subject\\\": commit_subject(root, c)})\\n947\\t\\n948\\t    counts = f\\\"{len(recorded)} recorded, {len(ordinary)} ordinary, {len(unrecorded)} unrecorded\\\"\\n949\\t    evasions = boundary_evasions if boundary_paths else \\\"n/a\\\"\\n950\\t    extra = {\\\"recorded\\\": len(recorded), \\\"ordinary\\\": len(ordinary),\\n951\\t             \\\"unrecorded\\\": len(unrecorded), \\\"boundary_evasions\\\": evasions,\\n952\\t             \\\"before_window\\\": before_window,\\n953\\t             \\\"ordinary_commits\\\": ordinary_commits, \\\"unrecorded_commits\\\": unrecorded_commits}\\n954\\t    if unrecorded:\\n955\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"{unrecorded[-1][:12]} lacks a record; {counts}; boundary evasions: \\\"\\n956\\t                      f\\\"{evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\\\", **extra)\\n957\\t    return p.hold(f\\\"{counts}; boundary evasions: {evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\\\",\\n958\\t                  **extra)\\n959\\t\\n960\\t\\n961\\tADAPTER_EXIT_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^\\\\[adapter exited \\\\d+\\\\]$\\\")\\n962\\t\\n963\\t\\n964\\tdef _log_owes_tool_error(log: str | None) -> bool:\\n965\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"True when a log's last non-empty line is exactly an adapter-exit\\n966\\t    marker and every line before it parses as JSON -- an adapter's own\\n967\\t    event stream, never a tool's own words (issue #94's own specimen,\\n968\\t    tenant zero's attest/records/659/verify-01.log: codex's\\n969\\t    \\\"thread.started\\\" event, then nothing but \\\"[adapter exited 1]\\\" -- the\\n970\\t    tool's real error line dropped before this reached the log, issue\\n971\\t    #86's own bug in split_adapter_stdout). A log that is only the exit\\n972\\t    marker, nothing before it at all, still owes the same line.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n973\\t    if not log:\\n974\\t        return False\\n975\\t    lines = [l for l in log.splitlines() if l.strip()]\\n976\\t    if not lines or not ADAPTER_EXIT_RE.match(lines[-1]):\\n977\\t        return False\\n978\\t    for l in lines[:-1]:\\n979\\t        try:\\n980\\t            json.loads(l)\\n981\\t        except ValueError:\\n982\\t            return False\\n983\\t    return True\\n984\\t\\n985\\t\\n986\\tdef proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n987\\t    p = Proof(\\\"no-stop-lacks-cause\\\", \\\"no stop lacks its cause\\\")\\n988\\t    if m is None:\\n989\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\\\")\\n990\\t    records_rel = m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"records\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n991\\t    records_dir = root / records_rel\\n992\\t    if not records_dir.is_dir():\\n993\\t        return p.fail(f\\\"no records directory under {records_dir}\\\")\\n994\\t\\n995\\t    # issue #89's own window lesson, proof three's already: a record\\n996\\t    # before record_version 3 has no stop by construction (schema\\n997\\t    # versions 1 and 2 predate it) -- counted here, never refused.\\n998\\t    older = 0\\n999\\t    checked = 0\\n1000\\t    problems: list[str] = []\\n1001\\t    for item_dir in sorted(d for d in records_dir.iterdir() if d.is_dir()):\\n1002\\t        for stage in STOP_STAGES:\\n1003\\t            for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_dir, stage).items()):\\n1004\\t                if rec.get(\\\"record_version\\\", 1) < 3:\\n1005\\t                    older += 1\\n1006\\t                    continue\\n1007\\t                if rec.get(\\\"status\\\") == \\\"pass\\\":\\n1008\\t                    continue\\n1009\\t                checked += 1\\n1010\\t                name = f\\\"{stage}-{n:02d}\\\"\\n1011\\t                stop = rec.get(\\\"stop\\\")\\n1012\\t                if not stop:\\n1013\\t                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} carries no stop\\\")\\n1014\\t                    continue\\n1015\\t                cls, provenance = stop.get(\\\"class\\\"), stop.get(\\\"provenance\\\")\\n1016\\t                if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\\n1017\\t                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \\\"\\n1018\\t                                    f\\\"no enumerated class\\\")\\n1019\\t                    continue\\n1020\\t                if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\\n1021\\t                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \\\"\\n1022\\t                                    f\\\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\\\")\\n1023\\t                    continue\\n1024\\t                if cls == \\\"unclassed\\\" and not stop.get(\\\"detail\\\"):\\n1025\\t                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is unclassed with no detail\\\")\\n1026\\t                    continue\\n1027\\t                log_path = item_dir / f\\\"{name}.log\\\"\\n1028\\t                log = log_path.read_text() if log_path.is_file() else None\\n1029\\t                # Issue #89, rejection test 1's own specimen (tenant\\n1030\\t                # zero's #659 build-01): a failed build that actually ran\\n1031\\t                # the gates -- selected_tests is set only once cmd_build\\n1032\\t                # reaches them -- owes their heading in the log, whatever\\n1033\\t                # else stop already says.\\n1034\\t                if (stage == \\\"build\\\" and rec.get(\\\"status\\\") == \\\"failed\\\"\\n1035\\t                        and rec.get(\\\"selected_tests\\\") is not None\\n1036\\t                        and \\\"--- attavo gates, iteration\\\" not in (log or \\\"\\\")):\\n1037\\t                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} failed after the gates ran \\\"\\n1038\\t                                    f\\\"but its log carries no gates heading\\\")\\n1039\\t                    continue\\n1040\\t                if _log_owes_tool_error(log):\\n1041\\t                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name}'s log ends in an adapter \\\"\\n1042\\t                                    f\\\"exit with nothing before it but event lines; the tool's \\\"\\n1043\\t                                    f\\\"own error line is owed\\\")\\n1044\\t\\n1045\\t        # issue #137: a refused spec-gate record is a stop too, class\\n1046\\t        # \\\"gate\\\" -- synthesized the same way item_stops and\\n1047\\t        # cmd_file_stops already read it, since cmd_spec_gate itself\\n1048\\t        # carries no stop field to check for one. No record_version\\n1049\\t        # gate here: unlike build/verify's own stop field, gate is never\\n1050\\t        # persisted, so there is no older shape that predates it.\\n1051\\t        for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_dir, \\\"spec\\\").items()):\\n1052\\t            if rec.get(\\\"status\\\") != \\\"refused\\\":\\n1053\\t                continue\\n1054\\t            checked += 1\\n1055\\t            name = f\\\"spec-{n:02d}\\\"\\n1056\\t            stop = gate_stop(rec.get(\\\"refusal\\\"))\\n1057\\t            cls, provenance = stop[\\\"class\\\"], stop[\\\"provenance\\\"]\\n1058\\t            if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\\n1059\\t                problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \\\"\\n1060\\t                                f\\\"no enumerated class\\\")\\n1061\\t                continue\\n1062\\t            if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\\n1063\\t                problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \\\"\\n1064\\t                                f\\\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\\\")\\n1065\\t                continue\\n1066\\t            if not stop.get(\\\"detail\\\"):\\n1067\\t                problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is a gate stop with no cause\\\")\\n1068\\t\\n1069\\t    older_note = f\\\"{older} record(s) before stop was recorded\\\"\\n1070\\t    if problems:\\n1071\\t        return p.fail(\\\"; \\\".join(problems), older_records=older)\\n1072\\t    return p.hold(f\\\"{checked} checked ({older_note})\\\" if checked == 0\\n1073\\t                 else f\\\"{checked} non-pass record(s) carry stop with a cause ({older_note})\\\",\\n1074\\t                 older_records=older)\\n1075\\t\\n1076\\t\\n1077\\tdef doctor(root: Path) -> list[Proof]:\\n1078\\t    m = read_manifest(root)\\n1079\\t    return [proof_every_gate_rejects(root, m),\\n1080\\t            proof_one_item_every_stage(root, m),\\n1081\\t            proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\\n1082\\t            proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m)]\\n1083\\t\\n1084\\t\\n1085\\tdef cmd_doctor(argv: list[str]) -> int:\\n1086\\t    as_json = \\\"--json\\\" in argv\\n1087\\t    args = [a for a in argv if a != \\\"--json\\\"]\\n1088\\t    root = Path(args[0] if args else \\\".\\\").resolve()\\n1089\\t    proofs = doctor(root)\\n1090\\t    if as_json:\\n1091\\t        print(json.dumps({\\\"root\\\": str(root), \\\"done\\\": all(p.holds for p in proofs),\\n1092\\t                          \\\"proofs\\\": [p.as_dict() for p in proofs]}, indent=2))\\n1093\\t    else:\\n1094\\t        for i, p in enumerate(proofs, 1):\\n1095\\t            print(f\\\"proof {i} {p.key}: {'HOLDS' if p.holds else 'FAILS'}: {p.reason}\\\")\\n1096\\t        print(\\\"doctor: done\\\" if all(p.holds for p in proofs)\\n1097\\t              else f\\\"doctor: not done ({sum(not p.holds for p in proofs)} of \\\"\\n1098\\t                   f\\\"{len(proofs)} proofs fail)\\\")\\n1099\\t    return 0 if all(p.holds for p in proofs) else 1\\n1100\\t\\n1101\\t\\n1102\\t# --- the spec contract ---\\n1103\\t\\n1104\\tdef parse_spec(spec_md: Path) -> tuple[dict | None, str | None]:\\n1105\\t    lines = spec_md.read_text().splitlines()\\n1106\\t    heading_idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\\\"## \\\")]\\n1107\\t    headings = [lines[i].rstrip() for i in heading_idx]\\n1108\\t    expected = [\\\"## Problem\\\", \\\"## Claims\\\", \\\"## Criteria\\\"]\\n1109\\t    if headings != expected:\\n1110\\t        bad = next((h for h in headings if h not in expected), None)\\n1111\\t        if bad is None:\\n1112\\t            missing = [h for h in expected if h not in headings]\\n1113\\t            bad = missing[0] if missing else \\\"heading order\\\"\\n1114\\t        return None, f\\\"headings: found {headings or ['(none)']}, expected {expected} ({bad})\\\"\\n1115\\t    idx_problem, idx_claims, idx_criteria = heading_idx\\n1116\\t    claims = [l.strip()[2:].strip() for l in lines[idx_claims + 1:idx_criteria]\\n1117\\t              if l.strip().startswith(\\\"- \\\")]\\n1118\\t    criteria = []\\n1119\\t    for l in lines[idx_criteria + 1:]:\\n1120\\t        s = l.strip()\\n1121\\t        if not s.startswith(\\\"- \\\") or \\\":\\\" not in s:\\n1122\\t            continue\\n1123\\t        name = s[2:].split(\\\":\\\", 1)[0].strip()\\n1124\\t        criteria.append(name)\\n1125\\t    return {\\\"claims\\\": claims, \\\"criteria\\\": criteria}, None\\n1126\\t\\n1127\\t\\n1128\\tdef run_criterion(exe: Path, cwd: Path) -> int:\\n1129\\t    try:\\n1130\\t        run = subprocess.run([str(exe)], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True,\\n1131\\t                             timeout=CRITERION_TIMEOUT, check=False)\\n1132\\t        return run.returncode\\n1133\\t    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\\n1134\\t        return 124\\n1135\\t    except OSError:\\n1136\\t        return 126\\n1137\\t\\n1138\\t\\n1139\\tdef parse_removed(stub_dir: Path) -> list[str]:\\n1140\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The paths listed in stub/.removed, one per line, comments (lines\\n1141\\t    starting with #) and blank lines ignored. [] when the stub carries no\\n1142\\t    .removed at all.\\n1143\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n1144\\t    removed_file = stub_dir / \\\".removed\\\"\\n1145\\t    if not removed_file.is_file():\\n1146\\t        return []\\n1147\\t    paths = []\\n1148\\t    for line in removed_file.read_text().splitlines():\\n1149\\t        s = line.strip()\\n1150\\t        if not s or s.startswith(\\\"#\\\"):\\n1151\\t            continue\\n1152\\t        paths.append(s)\\n1153\\t    return paths\\n1154\\t\\n1155\\t\\n1156\\tdef removed_path_refusal(root: Path, stub_dir: Path, rel: str) -> str | None:\\n1157\\t    p = Path(rel)\\n1158\\t    if p.is_absolute() or \\\"..\\\" in p.parts:\\n1159\\t        return f\\\"stub/.removed names a path outside the tree: {rel}\\\"\\n1160\\t    if not (root / p).exists():\\n1161\\t        return f\\\"stub/.removed names a path not in the tree: {rel}\\\"\\n1162\\t    if (stub_dir / p).exists():\\n1163\\t        return f\\\"stub/.removed names a path the stub also supplies: {rel}\\\"\\n1164\\t    return None\\n1165\\t\\n1166\\t\\n1167\\tdef stub_removed_refusal(root: Path, spec_dir: Path) -> str | None:\\n1168\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validated by name, before any criterion runs -- a stub whose\\n1169\\t    .removed cannot be applied has no meaning to gate against.\\n1170\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n1171\\t    stub_dir = spec_dir / \\\"stub\\\"\\n1172\\t    for rel in parse_removed(stub_dir):\\n1173\\t        refusal = removed_path_refusal(root, stub_dir, rel)\\n1174\\t        if refusal:\\n1175\\t            return refusal\\n1176\\t    return None\\n1177\\t\\n1178\\t\\n1179\\tdef run_criteria(root: Path, spec_dir: Path, names: list[str]) -> list[dict]:\\n1180\\t    criteria_dir = spec_dir / \\\"criteria\\\"\\n1181\\t    stub_dir = spec_dir / \\\"stub\\\"\\n1182\\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\\n1183\\t        tree = Path(tmp) / \\\"tree\\\"\\n1184\\t        stubbed = Path(tmp) / \\\"stubbed\\\"\\n1185\\t        shutil.copytree(root, tree, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(\\\".git\\\"))\\n1186\\t        shutil.copytree(root, stubbed, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(\\\".git\\\"))\\n1187\\t        if stub_dir.is_dir():\\n1188\\t            shutil.copytree(stub_dir, stubbed, dirs_exist_ok=True)\\n1189\\t            for rel in parse_removed(stub_dir):\\n1190\\t                target = stubbed / rel\\n1191\\t                if target.is_dir():\\n1192\\t                    shutil.rmtree(target)\\n1193\\t                elif target.exists():\\n1194\\t                    target.unlink()\\n1195\\t            removed_marker = stubbed / \\\".removed\\\"\\n1196\\t            if removed_marker.exists():\\n1197\\t                removed_marker.unlink()\\n1198\\t        results = []\\n1199\\t        for name in names:\\n1200\\t            exe = criteria_dir / name\\n1201\\t            results.append({\\\"name\\\": name,\\n1202\\t                            \\\"on_tree\\\": run_criterion(exe, tree),\\n1203\\t                            \\\"on_stub\\\": run_criterion(exe, stubbed)})\\n1204\\t        return results\\n1205\\t\\n1206\\t\\n1207\\tdef commit_postdates(root: Path, earlier: str, later: str) -> bool:\\n1208\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whether later is a strict descendant of earlier on this branch.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n1209\\t    if earlier == later:\\n1210\\t        return False\\n1211\\t    run = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"merge-base\\\", \\\"--is-ancestor\\\", earlier, later],\\n1212\\t                         capture_output=True, check=False)\\n1213\\t    return run.returncode == 0\\n1214\\t\\n1215\\t\\n1216\\tdef cmd_spec_gate(argv: list[str]) -> int:\\n1217\\t    root = Path(\\\".\\\").resolve()\\n1218\\t    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\\n1219\\t    if not item_id:\\n1220\\t        print(\\\"attavo spec-gate: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\\\",\\n1221\\t              file=sys.stderr)\\n1222\\t        return 2\\n1223\\t    m = read_manifest(root)\\n1224\\t    if m is None:\\n1225\\t        print(f\\\"attavo spec-gate: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n1226\\t        return 2\\n1227\\t    specs_rel = m[\\\"paths\\\"][\\\"specs\\\"]\\n1228\\t    records_rel = m[\\\"paths\\\"][\\\"records\\\"]\\n1229\\t    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\\n1230\\t    spec_md = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n1231\\t    if not spec_md.is_file():\\n1232\\t        print(f\\\"attavo spec-gate: no spec at {spec_dir}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n1233\\t        return 2\\n1234\\t    spec_rel = str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id)\\n1235\\t    try:\\n1236\\t        spec_sha = last_commit_touching(root, spec_rel)\\n1237\\t    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\\n1238\\t        print(f\\\"attavo spec-gate: refused: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n1239\\t        return 2\\n1240\\t\\n1241\\t    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\\n1242\\t    try:\\n1243\\t        approved = approval_status(root, m, item_id) == \\\"valid\\\"\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d\",\"uuid\":\"49e684d5-1cdd-469b-8f4c-4107032f61d7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-17T19:40:44.817Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/bin/attavo\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"attavo: the command.\\n\\n    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\\n    attavo spec-gate [N]\\n    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\\n    attavo approval-status [N]\\n    attavo build [N]\\n    attavo verify [N]\\n    attavo file-findings [N]\\n    attavo file-stops [N]\\n    attavo counsel [N]\\n    attavo record-only\\n    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\\n    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready]\\n    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\\n    attavo stops [N] [--json]\\n\\nThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts four proofs against a\\ntenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\\n\\n  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\\n                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\\n                             and carries a non-empty retires\\n  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\\n                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\\n                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\\n                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\\n  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\\n                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\\n                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\\n                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\\n                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\\n                             carries its own record paths this way)\\n  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\\n                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\\n                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\\n                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\\n                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\\n                             heading when a build failed after running\\n                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\\n                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\\n                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\\n                             never refused\\n\\nNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\\nblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\\nis done.\\n\\nspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\\none enforces.\\n\\nbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\\ndeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\\napproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\\n(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\\nGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\\nconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\\nspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\\nbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\\nevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\\ndeclared \\\"reports\\\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\\nit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\\nnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\\nsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\\ntests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\\nwhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\\nwhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\\nthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\\nnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\\nbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\\nthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\\nexits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\\nunder an \\\"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\\\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\\nit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\\n{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\\nalready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\\nbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\\nenforces.\\n\\nverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\\nstatus pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\\na tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\\nline per check as \\\"<name> <conclusion>\\\". verify runs it on the build\\nrecord's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\\nskipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\\nadapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\\ncalled red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\\n[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\\nthe build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\\nfindings and its declared \\\"reports\\\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\\nbuild or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\\nATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\\nresult. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\\ncarries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\\ncarries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\\nthe item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\\nrefuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\\nretires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\\nfull rules both enforce.\\n\\nfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\\nissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\\nclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\\nlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\\nbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\\nfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\\nthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\\ncommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\\nnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\\nempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\\ncould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\\n\\ncounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\\nwhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\\npoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\\napproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\\n[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\\nread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\\nclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\\nitem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\\nroot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\\nsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\\nstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\\ncitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\\ndiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\\n(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\\nand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\\nthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\\ntranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\\ncaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\\nwritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\\nrecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\\nenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\\n\\nrecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\\npaths.records; 1 otherwise; 2 with no manifest. Core logic about a git\\ncheckout, not a forge's shell -- a workflow template's push-and-retrigger\\nguard is one line reading this exit code instead of carrying its own\\ncopy of the check.\\n\\nattest refuses (exit 1) unless the latest spec, approval, build, and\\nverify records for an item all exist and chain: the build's approval_sha\\nnames the latest approval, and the verify's build_sha names that build --\\na re-approval after a build must force a re-run of what changed. With no\\nN given it derives the item from the record paths HEAD's merge commit\\ntouched under paths.records/<N>/, not from a branch name, which a squash\\nmerge discards and which names a forge's convention the product does not\\nknow; more than one item derived is a refusal naming what it found. Zero\\nis not a defect -- not every merge is an item merge -- exit 0, nothing\\nprinted but a line saying so.\\n\\nattest never writes. On a coherent chain it prints the attestation\\nstatement -- validating against schema/attestation.schema.json -- to\\nstdout as JSON and exits 0: the item, its four records and their shas,\\nand the commit the statement was computed at (sha and merge_sha are the\\nsame commit here; on the merge group that commit is the one that lands).\\nThe four stage records already under paths.records are the evidence for\\nthat statement; a forge-specific template signs the printed JSON,\\nunmodified, as the predicate, against the commit that lands, on the merge\\ngroup -- and the signed bundle in the forge's attestation store is the\\nseal over it. attest itself never signs anything and never talks to a\\nsigning service. --partial (issue #67) is for a pull request, where the\\nrecord a complete chain would need is the output of a later stage that is\\nitself waiting on this check: a missing later record is \\\"not yet\\\" (exit\\n0, naming the item and the stages present and absent, no statement\\nprinted) rather than a refusal, while the two chain assertions -- build's\\napproval_sha names the latest approval, verify's build_sha names the\\nlatest build -- still run over whatever records exist. merge_group and a\\npush to main still demand the whole chain. See issue #69's lane for the\\nfull rules it enforces.\\n\\ndrive reads an item's latest records and a forge's own check conclusions\\nand performs the next mechanical step, and only that step, then stops: no\\nvalid approval refuses by name and runs nothing; no passing build bound to\\nthat approval runs build; a passing build with the forge green on the\\nbranch head (polled for a bound, not the manifest) runs verify; a passing\\nverify with the forge still green prints that the item is ready to merge\\nand stops there -- the merge is never drive's own act, and it enqueues\\nnothing. A record build or verify writes that is not pass is counseled (counsel,\\nissue #100) and filed (file-stops, issue #89) before it is transported,\\nso its .filed marker exists in time to be committed alongside it; drive\\nthen commits the stage record and the counsel record together -- each\\nwith its own log and marker -- with `git commit --only`, never sweeping\\nthe index, and pushes; a push a divergent remote rejects\\nis retried once after `git pull --no-rebase --no-edit`, never a rebase,\\nsince the record already names the commit's sha. drive writes no record\\nof its own: a second run in the same state repeats the same step or the\\nsame stop, reading exactly what the prior run left behind -- the marker\\nincluded, so a stop already filed is never filed again, from this\\nworktree or a fresh one. See issue #84's lane for the full rules it\\nenforces.\\n\\n--until-ready (issue #100's own followups) repeats step-and-wait --\\nstep, the forge poll already inside a step, step again -- in the same\\nprocess, rather than making the caller invoke drive again after every\\npassing step, until the item is ready to merge or a step stops on its\\nown account (a refusal, a halted or failed or refused record, or the\\nforge never going green); a step that stops still prints exactly what\\nthe same step would print without the flag. Without --until-ready,\\ndrive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\\n\\nledger reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\\npaths.records when N is omitted), it walks the commits from the item's\\nfirst spec commit to its merge (the same derivation doctor's proof two\\nand attest use) or to HEAD when the item has not merged, and prints one\\nrow per act: the sha, the identity as git names it, and a class from a\\nclosed list -- spec, amend, approve, launch, record, change, transport,\\nmerge -- derived from who committed it and, for an approval, build, or\\nverify record, what the record itself says. A summary line follows:\\noperator acts (approve, amend, launch, transport, merge), product acts\\n(record), executor commits (change), stops (non-pass records), and\\nsince (the product version on the first record). A build or verify\\nrecord's own commit, from before v0.18.0 gave the driver and the\\nexecutor their own identities, prints as record-or-launch with a note,\\ncounted toward neither total, rather than guessed. --json prints the\\nrows and the summary as one object. See issue #128's lane for the full\\nrules it enforces.\\n\\nstops reads, never writes. For item N (or every item under\\npaths.records when N is omitted), one row per non-pass build or verify\\nrecord: the record, its stop's class, provenance, and detail, and the\\nanswerer -- \\\"counsel:<verdict>\\\" when a counsel record read this exact\\nstop, else \\\"person\\\" for a question, else \\\"guard\\\" for a class a guard\\nalone raised (GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES), else \\\"none\\\". A record too old to\\ncarry stop at all prints the doctor's own phrase for it, \\\"before stop\\nwas recorded\\\", and is counted there rather than by class. Totals per\\nclass (read from the build record schema's own enum, never retyped) and\\nper answerer, plus the before-stop count, follow the rows. --json prints\\nthe rows and the totals as one object. See issue #129's lane for the\\nfull rules it enforces.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport fnmatch\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport re\\nimport shlex\\nimport shutil\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nimport tempfile\\nimport time\\nimport tomllib\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nMANIFEST = \\\"attavo.toml\\\"\\nSTAGES = (\\\"spec\\\", \\\"approval\\\", \\\"build\\\", \\\"verify\\\")\\nCRITERION_TIMEOUT = 120\\nRECORD_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^([a-z]+)-([0-9]{2,})\\\\.json$\\\")\\nBUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET = 3\\nBUILD_HALT_EXIT = 3\\nCHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES = 200\\nPRODUCT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\\n# issue #84: a constant the lane names, not a manifest key, until a tenant\\n# disagrees -- how long drive gives a forge's checks room to conclude\\n# before it gives up and stops rather than call a judge on a tree the\\n# forge has not yet finished reading. Tenant zero's own checks conclude\\n# about five minutes after a push; the default bound gives them room to\\n# finish so a person is not the one re-running drive after CI, which is\\n# exactly the transport act this lane retires. ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\\n# and ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S, read at call time rather than once at\\n# import, are for a test's own clock, not a tenant's -- there is no\\n# manifest key for either.\\nDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S = 600.0\\nDRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S = 20.0\\n\\n\\ndef drive_forge_poll_bound_s() -> float:\\n    return float(os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S\\\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_BOUND_DEFAULT_S))\\n\\n\\ndef drive_forge_poll_interval_s() -> float:\\n    return float(os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\\\", DRIVE_FORGE_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT_S))\\n\\n\\nclass Proof:\\n    def __init__(self, key: str, title: str) -> None:\\n        self.key = key\\n        self.title = title\\n        self.holds = False\\n        self.reason = \\\"\\\"\\n        self.extra: dict = {}\\n\\n    def fail(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \\\"Proof\\\":\\n        self.holds, self.reason = False, reason\\n        self.extra.update(extra)\\n        return self\\n\\n    def hold(self, reason: str, **extra) -> \\\"Proof\\\":\\n        self.holds, self.reason = True, reason\\n        self.extra.update(extra)\\n        return self\\n\\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\\"proof\\\": self.key, \\\"title\\\": self.title,\\n                \\\"holds\\\": self.holds, \\\"reason\\\": self.reason, **self.extra}\\n\\n\\ndef read_manifest(root: Path) -> dict | None:\\n    path = root / MANIFEST\\n    if not path.is_file():\\n        return None\\n    with path.open(\\\"rb\\\") as fh:\\n        return tomllib.load(fh)\\n\\n\\ndef git(root: Path, *args: str, env: dict | None = None) -> str:\\n    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), *args],\\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\\n    if out.returncode != 0:\\n        raise RuntimeError(out.stderr.strip() or \\\"git failed\\\")\\n    return out.stdout\\n\\n\\ndef product_version() -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"What the running program is. Three fallbacks, in order, and never an\\n    exception -- this runs inside write_record, after the work it\\n    describes already happened, and a raise here would lose the record\\n    for an invocation that already ran:\\n\\n      1. ATTAVO_PRODUCT_VERSION, when the environment sets it. The forge\\n         action sets this from its own ref (action.yml, not here -- this\\n         function stays forge-agnostic).\\n      2. git describe --tags --always --dirty against PRODUCT_ROOT: a\\n         tagged release reports its tag, a checkout reports its commit,\\n         a dirty tree says so.\\n      3. \\\"unknown\\\", when PRODUCT_ROOT is not a git repository at all --\\n         the case for a forge that extracts this action from a tarball\\n         rather than a git checkout, which is exactly when (1) is\\n         expected to already have supplied the answer.\\n\\n    Distinct from the tenant's product_pin -- an operator running a\\n    checkout, which is how every build and verify have actually been run\\n    so far, bypasses the pin entirely (issue #49).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    env = os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_PRODUCT_VERSION\\\")\\n    if env:\\n        return env\\n    try:\\n        return git(PRODUCT_ROOT, \\\"describe\\\", \\\"--tags\\\", \\\"--always\\\", \\\"--dirty\\\").strip()\\n    except RuntimeError:\\n        return \\\"unknown\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef now_iso() -> str:\\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef derive_item_id(root: Path) -> str | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"ATTAVO_ITEM first, not last: a rejection fixture's own item id must\\n    win over whatever attavo/N-* branch the enclosing tenant repository\\n    happens to be checked out on -- the common case is doctor running from\\n    a real item's own branch, where a fallback-only env var would never be\\n    consulted at all and every gate fixture would silently resolve to the\\n    real item instead of its own.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    env_item = os.environ.get(\\\"ATTAVO_ITEM\\\")\\n    if env_item:\\n        return env_item\\n    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--abbrev-ref\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\"],\\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n    branch = out.stdout.strip()\\n    m = re.match(r\\\"^attavo/(\\\\d+)-\\\", branch)\\n    return m.group(1) if m else None\\n\\n\\ndef fixture_item_id(fixture: Path) -> str | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one item id under a rejection fixture's own paths.specs, so the\\n    doctor can export it as ATTAVO_ITEM: a fixture carries no attavo/N-*\\n    branch for a gate command with no argument to derive from otherwise.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    fm = read_manifest(fixture)\\n    specs_rel = ((fm or {}).get(\\\"paths\\\") or {}).get(\\\"specs\\\")\\n    if not specs_rel:\\n        return None\\n    specs_dir = fixture / specs_rel\\n    if not specs_dir.is_dir():\\n        return None\\n    items = sorted(p.name for p in specs_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir())\\n    return items[0] if len(items) == 1 else None\\n\\n\\nclass ShallowCheckoutError(RuntimeError):\\n    pass\\n\\n\\ndef last_commit_touching(root: Path, relpath: str) -> str | None:\\n    shallow = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--is-shallow-repository\\\"],\\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n    if shallow.stdout.strip() == \\\"true\\\":\\n        raise ShallowCheckoutError(\\n            \\\"shallow checkout: git log -1 -- <path> returns HEAD for every path on a \\\"\\n            \\\"shallow clone; check out with fetch-depth: 0\\\")\\n    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"log\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\", \\\"--\\\", relpath],\\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n    sha = out.stdout.strip()\\n    return sha or None\\n\\n\\n# --- record files: <stage>-NN.json, one per attempt, never overwritten ---\\n\\nSCHEMA_RECORDS_DIR = PRODUCT_ROOT / \\\"schema\\\" / \\\"records\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef stage_schema(stage: str) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"schema/records/<stage>.schema.json -- this repository's own\\n    declaration of that stage's record shape (issue #60). The only\\n    artifact the outbound contract needs; there is no accessor for it\\n    beyond reading the file.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return json.loads((SCHEMA_RECORDS_DIR / f\\\"{stage}.schema.json\\\").read_text())\\n\\n\\ndef schema_id_version(schema: dict) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The trailing integer of a schema's $id (\\\".../records/build/2\\\" -> 2)\\n    -- the single place a record shape's version lives. write_record reads\\n    this at call time rather than carrying its own copy, so the version it\\n    stamps cannot drift from what the schema declares (issue #60).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return int(schema[\\\"$id\\\"].rsplit(\\\"/\\\", 1)[-1])\\n\\n\\nclass RecordItemMismatch(RuntimeError):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A record's item field disagrees with the directory it was read\\n    from (issue #60, acceptance 5) -- a misfiled or copied record, refused\\n    rather than trusted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _load_record(path: Path, item_id: str) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one place in this repository that turns a record file's bytes\\n    into a dict (issue #60, acceptance 6). Defaults record_version to 1\\n    when absent -- version 1 is every record written before this release\\n    and is never migrated -- and fills item from the directory when\\n    absent; refuses when a present item disagrees with it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    data = json.loads(path.read_text())\\n    data.setdefault(\\\"record_version\\\", 1)\\n    item = data.get(\\\"item\\\")\\n    if item is None:\\n        data[\\\"item\\\"] = item_id\\n    elif item != item_id:\\n        raise RecordItemMismatch(\\n            f\\\"{path}: item {item!r} disagrees with its directory {item_id!r}\\\")\\n    return data\\n\\n\\ndef parse_attempts(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> dict[int, dict]:\\n    attempts: dict[int, dict] = {}\\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\\n        return attempts\\n    for f in records_dir.glob(f\\\"{stage}-*.json\\\"):\\n        m = RECORD_RE.match(f.name)\\n        if not m or m.group(1) != stage:\\n            continue\\n        try:\\n            attempts[int(m.group(2))] = _load_record(f, records_dir.name)\\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n            continue\\n    return attempts\\n\\n\\ndef latest_record(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> dict | None:\\n    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\\n    return attempts[max(attempts)] if attempts else None\\n\\n\\ndef next_attempt_number(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> int:\\n    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\\n    return (max(attempts) + 1) if attempts else 1\\n\\n\\ndef latest_attempt_path(records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> Path | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The path of the highest-numbered <stage>-NN.json, or None.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, stage)\\n    if not attempts:\\n        return None\\n    return records_dir / f\\\"{stage}-{max(attempts):02d}.json\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef write_record(records_dir: Path, stage: str, record: dict, m: dict, item: str,\\n                 log: str | None = None) -> Path:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every record gains record_version (this stage schema's own $id\\n    version -- issue #60) and item (verbatim from the caller, matching the\\n    record's directory segment), plus product_version (what ran, derived\\n    here) and product_pin (what the tenant declared, copied verbatim from\\n    the manifest, or null when the manifest carries no [attavo] table) --\\n    the latter two recorded, never enforced (issue #49). A manifest\\n    missing the table is an absent fact, not a crash: this is the one\\n    caller of write_record that must not raise on a shape the manifest\\n    schema forbids but tomllib.load happily returns.\\n\\n    Refuses (raises ValueError) a record carrying a key this stage's\\n    schema does not declare -- the declared key set enforced with the\\n    standard library, not a jsonschema import: bin/attavo is a single\\n    script a tenant pins, and a runtime dependency changes installation.\\n\\n    Also refuses a `status: \\\"failed\\\"` record that carries no trail at all\\n    -- log the empty or missing text it will sit beside, and refusal and\\n    halted (where the stage's schema has them) both null (issue #53).\\n    `returned`, `pass`, `halted`, and `refused` owe no such trail. log is\\n    None for a stage that invoked no adapter (verify's `returned`), which\\n    write_record then writes no log file for; otherwise the log is\\n    written before the record, so a refusal leaves no half-pair.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    records_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\\n    schema = stage_schema(stage)\\n    record = {**record, \\\"record_version\\\": schema_id_version(schema), \\\"item\\\": item,\\n              \\\"product_version\\\": product_version(),\\n              \\\"product_pin\\\": (m.get(\\\"attavo\\\") or {}).get(\\\"version\\\")}\\n    undeclared = set(record) - set(schema.get(\\\"properties\\\", {}))\\n    if undeclared:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"write_record: {stage} record carries key(s) its schema does not \\\"\\n                         f\\\"declare: {', '.join(sorted(undeclared))}\\\")\\n    if (record.get(\\\"status\\\") == \\\"failed\\\" and not log\\n            and record.get(\\\"refusal\\\") is None and record.get(\\\"halted\\\") is None):\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"write_record: {stage} record status is 'failed' with no log, \\\"\\n                         f\\\"refusal, or halted to say why\\\")\\n    path = records_dir / f\\\"{stage}-{nn:02d}.json\\\"\\n    if log is not None:\\n        path.with_suffix(\\\".log\\\").write_text(log)\\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n    return path\\n\\n\\n# --- stop: every non-pass build or verify record's class and cause (issue\\n# #89) -- derived here, at write time, from the refusal, halted, and log\\n# the caller already has. Never a fresh read of anything: the tenant zero\\n# specimens this retires (#576 build-11, #659 build-01 and verify-01) are\\n# exactly a stop the product wrote with nothing beside it to explain\\n# itself after the fact. ---\\n\\nSTOP_CLASSES = (\\\"non-question\\\", \\\"outlived-invocation\\\", \\\"no-cause\\\", \\\"forge-unconcluded\\\",\\n               \\\"ceiling\\\", \\\"claims-boundary\\\", \\\"repeated-act\\\", \\\"unclassed\\\", \\\"question\\\",\\n               \\\"environment\\\", \\\"gate\\\")\\nSTOP_PROVENANCES = (\\\"product\\\", \\\"tenant\\\", \\\"executor\\\", \\\"spec\\\")\\n\\n# Beyond the enum spelling itself, the prose issue #88 actually shipped\\n# (adapters/claude-code/run and adapters/codex/run, on main since\\n# v0.16.0) once put a class's own name, or a real specimen's wording of\\n# it, in the transcript for the generic match below to find. Issue #94\\n# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\\n# (below): non-question's own halt line (\\\"halted: class non-question\\\")\\n# would otherwise still satisfy the bare-name match here with no adapter\\n# report-line field involved at all, and outlived-invocation's refusal\\n# never named its class in text to begin with, so both are disabled here\\n# -- the same pattern issue #93 established for ceiling, just below,\\n# rather than removed outright.\\nCLASS_TEXT_MARKERS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\\n    \\\"non-question\\\": (),\\n    \\\"outlived-invocation\\\": (),\\n    # Issue #93: ceiling's own text-based check is CEILING_MARKERS, below,\\n    # with provenance \\\"product\\\" -- a fact about the tool, not an executor\\n    # judgment like non-question/outlived-invocation are. Left at the\\n    # default (the class's own name, \\\"ceiling\\\"), the generic match above\\n    # would instead catch adapters/codex/run's and\\n    # adapters/claude-code/run's own pre-emptive refusal -- which must\\n    # carry the word \\\"ceiling\\\" by the same issue's own brief -- as\\n    # provenance \\\"executor\\\", before CEILING_MARKERS is ever consulted.\\n    \\\"ceiling\\\": (),\\n    # A genuine question (issue #100's own followups) is read structurally\\n    # -- status \\\"halted\\\" carrying a non-empty halted.question -- not by\\n    # scanning for the literal word \\\"question\\\", which the question's own\\n    # text very often contains regardless of what it is actually asking.\\n    # Left at the default, the generic match above would misclassify any\\n    # question that happens to use the word \\\"question\\\" as executor\\n    # provenance, before the structural check in derive_stop is reached.\\n    \\\"question\\\": (),\\n    # environment/tenant (issue #115) is set directly by cmd_build's own\\n    # preflight -- the one caller who knows a [checks].command exited 2\\n    # on the approved tree -- never derived from adapter text. Left at\\n    # the default, the generic match above would catch the word\\n    # \\\"environment\\\" anywhere in a log or refusal (e.g. codex's own\\n    # OPENAI_API_KEY auth-mismatch refusal, adapters/codex/run's\\n    # check_auth) as an environment/executor stop that never happened.\\n    \\\"environment\\\": (),\\n}\\n\\n# Known tool error text for a declared ceiling -- issue #86's own specimen\\n# (codex's \\\"Input exceeds...\\\" line on a diff too large to judge) is\\n# \\\"input_too_large\\\"; a matching line anywhere in the log, not only its\\n# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \\\"[adapter exited\\n# N]\\\" after whatever the tool itself printed. \\\"ceiling exceeded\\\" is issue\\n# #93's own addition: both adapters now refuse pre-emptively, before the\\n# tool is ever invoked, against a declared or fixed input limit, and\\n# their refusal text is not caught by any of the three markers above.\\nCEILING_MARKERS = (\\\"input_too_large\\\", \\\"exceeds the maximum context length\\\",\\n                  \\\"context_length_exceeded\\\", \\\"ceiling exceeded\\\")\\n\\n\\n# Issue #100's followups: an unclassed detail is the log's last line\\n# verbatim, and that line is sometimes an adapter's own event JSON or a\\n# tool's full error text -- thousands of characters wide. Capped here,\\n# at write time, so a filed issue's own summary of it (file-stops'\\n# log_tail already carries the full picture) stays short; the class\\n# itself, \\\"unclassed\\\", already says the full explanation lives in the\\n# log, not in this field.\\nUNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS = 200\\n\\n\\ndef _log_last_line(log: str | None) -> str:\\n    lines = [l for l in (log or \\\"\\\").splitlines() if l.strip()]\\n    last = lines[-1] if lines else \\\"\\\"\\n    return last[:UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS]\\n\\n\\ndef _carries_a_known_class(text: str | None) -> str | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whichever of STOP_CLASSES this text names -- its own spelling, or\\n    one of CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS' real-world phrasings of it, when that\\n    class is not disabled there -- or None. Issue #88 is where an\\n    adapter's own halt or refusal first named its class this way; issue\\n    #93 added ceiling's own pre-emptive refusal to that set and disabled\\n    its bare-name match (CEILING_MARKERS covers it instead); issue #94\\n    disables non-question and outlived-invocation the same way, reading\\n    both from the adapter's own report line (derive_stop's report_class)\\n    now instead.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = text or \\\"\\\"\\n    for name in STOP_CLASSES:\\n        markers = CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS.get(name, (name,))\\n        if any(marker in text for marker in markers):\\n            return name\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef derive_stop(status: str, *, refusal: str | None = None, halted: dict | None = None,\\n                log: str | None = None, report_class: str | None = None,\\n                refusal_provenance: str | None = None) -> dict | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The stop field for a build or verify record: None for status \\\"pass\\\",\\n    else {class, provenance, detail} from what the caller already knows.\\n\\n      - report_class -- payload.get(\\\"class\\\") off the adapter's own report\\n        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\\n        that class, provenance \\\"executor\\\". build.schema.json and\\n        verify.schema.json stay untouched by issue #88 on purpose, so the\\n        class lives only on the report line, never a structured field\\n        cmd_build or cmd_verify forwards on its own account; the caller\\n        reads payload itself and passes this in, since only it still has\\n        payload once an iteration ends. This is non-question's and\\n        outlived-invocation's only path to a record now (issue #94):\\n        CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS disables both for the text scan below, the\\n        same way issue #93 disabled ceiling's bare-name match there. A\\n        class an adapter does not yet put on its report line --\\n        outlived-invocation today, since that refusal path prints no\\n        report line at all -- falls to unclassed below, same as any\\n        other unnamed cause, until the adapter that raises it puts a\\n        class on the line the way non-question already does.\\n      - a halt carrying a non-empty halted.question, once it is not a\\n        non-question caught above, is a genuine question -- question/spec,\\n        with the question's own first line as detail (issue #100's\\n        followups). This is the specimen issue #100 itself was built to\\n        retire: tenant zero's #663 build-01, a proper question, classed\\n        unclassed/product and filed as a product defect with the wrong\\n        provenance -- a question is about the definition of done, which is\\n        a person's or a ruling's to answer, never the product's own\\n        mechanism.\\n      - failing that, a refusal or the log itself that already names its\\n        class in text (issue #88, #93 for ceiling's own pre-emptive\\n        refusal) is that class, provenance \\\"executor\\\" -- the log is\\n        checked because neither adapter's refusal *field* carries the\\n        class today; the class-naming line each adapter prints reaches\\n        only the transcript\\n      - a refusal that is not that -- the write-outside-claims path\\n        itself, not the \\\"commit ... not authored by the executor\\\" shape\\n        -- is claims-boundary/spec, unless the caller already knows this\\n        refusal touched paths.records or paths.specs (issue #140:\\n        protected_path_touched, checked ahead of the ordinary claims\\n        match in cmd_build) and passes refusal_provenance=\\\"executor\\\" --\\n        the product's own directories are not a claim a spec makes, so a\\n        refusal there is not the spec's boundary to answer for\\n      - a returned verify (the forge was not green; no adapter ran) is\\n        forge-unconcluded/tenant\\n      - an adapter exit whose log carries a declared-ceiling error line is\\n        ceiling/product\\n      - anything else is unclassed/product, with the log's last line\\n        (capped at UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS) as its detail -- the other\\n        class that carries a detail, since every remaining class's\\n        evidence already lives in refusal, halted, forge_checks, or the\\n        log itself.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if status == \\\"pass\\\":\\n        return None\\n    if status == \\\"returned\\\":\\n        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"forge-unconcluded\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"tenant\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\\n        return {\\\"class\\\": report_class, \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"executor\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n    question = (halted or {}).get(\\\"question\\\")\\n    if status == \\\"halted\\\" and question:\\n        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"question\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"spec\\\",\\n               \\\"detail\\\": question.splitlines()[0]}\\n    known = _carries_a_known_class(refusal) or _carries_a_known_class(log)\\n    if known:\\n        return {\\\"class\\\": known, \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"executor\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n    if status == \\\"refused\\\" and refusal is not None and not refusal.startswith(\\\"commit \\\"):\\n        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"claims-boundary\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": refusal_provenance or \\\"spec\\\",\\n               \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n    if log and any(marker in log.lower() for marker in CEILING_MARKERS):\\n        return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"ceiling\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"product\\\", \\\"detail\\\": None}\\n    return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"unclassed\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"product\\\", \\\"detail\\\": _log_last_line(log)}\\n\\n\\ndef gate_stop(refusal: str | None) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The stop for a refused spec-gate record: class \\\"gate\\\", provenance\\n    \\\"spec\\\", the refusal string itself as cause (issue #137) -- not\\n    derive_stop's generic claims-boundary/spec fallback issue #133\\n    reused, which named a boundary the record never crossed: \\\"criterion\\n    fails against the tree plus stub: doctor-template-absent.sh\\\" is not\\n    a write outside claims. cmd_spec_gate is untouched by this lane, so\\n    a spec record still carries no stop field of its own; this is\\n    synthesized wherever a refused one is read (item_stops,\\n    cmd_file_stops, proof_no_stop_lacks_cause), never persisted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return {\\\"class\\\": \\\"gate\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": \\\"spec\\\", \\\"detail\\\": refusal}\\n\\n\\ndef load_records(records_dir: Path) -> dict[str, dict[str, dict]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"{item_id: {stage: latest_record}} for every <records>/<item>/<stage>-NN.json.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    items: dict[str, dict[str, dict]] = {}\\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\\n        return items\\n    for item_dir in sorted(p for p in records_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir()):\\n        by_stage: dict[str, dict[int, dict]] = {}\\n        for rec in sorted(item_dir.glob(\\\"*.json\\\")):\\n            m = RECORD_RE.match(rec.name)\\n            if not m:\\n                continue\\n            stage, n = m.group(1), int(m.group(2))\\n            try:\\n                data = _load_record(rec, item_dir.name)\\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                continue\\n            by_stage.setdefault(stage, {})[n] = data\\n        items[item_dir.name] = {stage: attempts[max(attempts)] for stage, attempts in by_stage.items()}\\n    return items\\n\\n\\n# --- doctor's three proofs ---\\n\\ndef proof_every_gate_rejects(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n    p = Proof(\\\"every-gate-rejects\\\", \\\"every gate rejects its fixture\\\")\\n    if m is None:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no gate is registered\\\")\\n    gates = m.get(\\\"gates\\\") or {}\\n    if not gates:\\n        return p.fail(\\\"[gates] is empty; a gate that has rejected nothing does not exist\\\")\\n    fixtures = root / m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"rejections\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    # Proposal, not yet ruled on (issue #54): a gate that retires nothing\\n    # only adds, so proof one reports it here rather than waiting on the\\n    # schema alone -- read_manifest never validates against the manifest\\n    # schema at runtime, so a schema requirement is not an enforced one.\\n    no_retires = [name for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()) if not gate.get(\\\"retires\\\")]\\n    missing, accepted = [], []\\n    for name, gate in sorted(gates.items()):\\n        fixture = fixtures / name\\n        if not fixture.is_dir():\\n            missing.append(name)\\n            continue\\n        env = dict(os.environ)\\n        item = fixture_item_id(fixture)\\n        if item is not None:\\n            env[\\\"ATTAVO_ITEM\\\"] = item\\n        run = subprocess.run(gate[\\\"command\\\"], shell=True, cwd=str(fixture),\\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=env)\\n        if run.returncode == 0:\\n            accepted.append(name)\\n    if missing:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"gate(s) with no rejection fixture: {', '.join(missing)}\\\")\\n    if accepted:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"gate(s) that accepted their rejection fixture: {', '.join(accepted)}\\\")\\n    if no_retires:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"gate(s) with no retires: {', '.join(no_retires)}\\\")\\n    return p.hold(f\\\"{len(gates)} gate(s) rejected their fixture\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef merge_introducing_records(root: Path, records_rel: str, item: str,\\n                              stages: tuple[str, ...]) -> str | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The merge commit reachable from HEAD whose first-parent diff\\n    introduces a record for every one of stages, under\\n    records_rel/item/ -- the same derivation attest itself uses\\n    (derive_attest_items), read here so proof two requires an item's\\n    stage records to have arrived by an actual merge, not merely to sit\\n    in the tree (issue #69, acceptance row 4).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        merges = git(root, \\\"log\\\", \\\"--merges\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\").split()\\n    except RuntimeError:\\n        return None\\n    prefix = f\\\"{records_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item}/\\\"\\n    for sha in merges:\\n        try:\\n            diff = git(root, \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", f\\\"{sha}^1\\\", sha).splitlines()\\n        except RuntimeError:\\n            continue\\n        found: set[str] = set()\\n        for p in diff:\\n            if p.startswith(prefix):\\n                m = RECORD_RE.match(Path(p).name)\\n                if m:\\n                    found.add(m.group(1))\\n        if all(s in found for s in stages):\\n            return sha\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef proof_one_item_every_stage(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n    p = Proof(\\\"one-item-every-stage\\\", \\\"one item has traversed every stage\\\")\\n    if m is None:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\\\")\\n    records_rel = m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"records\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\\n    items = load_records(records_dir)\\n    if not items:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no work item under {records_dir.relative_to(root)}\\\")\\n    complete = [item for item, stages in items.items() if all(s in stages for s in STAGES)]\\n    if not complete:\\n        best = max(items.items(), key=lambda kv: len(kv[1]))\\n        lacking = [s for s in STAGES if s not in best[1]]\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no item carries every stage; item {best[0]} lacks {', '.join(lacking)}\\\")\\n\\n    # issue #74: a complete item is counted only when its chain holds --\\n    # attavo attest refuses a build re-approved after the fact or a\\n    # verify whose build went stale, and the coherence gate refuses the\\n    # merge group on exactly that; a proof that never asked would call a\\n    # traversal the gate itself would not let through. The refusal text\\n    # is check_attest_chain's own, never re-typed here.\\n    refused, held, unmerged = [], [], []\\n    for item in complete:\\n        chain, message = check_attest_chain(records_dir / item, item)\\n        if chain is None:\\n            refused.append(f\\\"item {item}: {message}\\\")\\n            continue\\n        merge_sha = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item, STAGES)\\n        if merge_sha:\\n            held.append((item, merge_sha))\\n        else:\\n            unmerged.append(item)\\n\\n    if held:\\n        names = \\\", \\\".join(item for item, _ in held)\\n        shas = \\\", \\\".join(sha[:12] for _, sha in held)\\n        return p.hold(f\\\"item(s) {names} carry {', '.join(STAGES)} with the chain held, \\\"\\n                      f\\\"merged at {shas}\\\")\\n    if refused:\\n        return p.fail(\\\"; \\\".join(refused))\\n    return p.fail(f\\\"item(s) {', '.join(unmerged)} carry every stage with the chain held but no \\\"\\n                  f\\\"merge commit's first-parent diff introduces all of them\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef commit_subject(root: Path, sha: str) -> str:\\n    return git(root, \\\"log\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--format=%s\\\", sha).strip()\\n\\n\\ndef touches_boundary(root: Path, sha: str, boundary_paths: list[str]) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whether sha's first-parent diff touches a path [spec.boundary].paths\\n    declares governed -- an ordinary merge that does is a boundary\\n    evasion (issue #72): the tenant carried a governed change around the\\n    path the manifest itself names.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    diff = git(root, \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", f\\\"{sha}^1\\\", sha).splitlines()\\n    return any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, pattern) for path in diff for pattern in boundary_paths)\\n\\n\\ndef proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n    p = Proof(\\\"no-commit-lacks-record\\\", \\\"no commit lacks a record\\\")\\n    if m is None:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; the tenant has no record boundary\\\")\\n    try:\\n        install = git(root, \\\"log\\\", \\\"--diff-filter=A\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\",\\n                      \\\"--reverse\\\", \\\"--\\\", MANIFEST).split()\\n    except RuntimeError as exc:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"git: {exc}\\\")\\n    if not install:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"{MANIFEST} is not committed; the tenant has no record boundary\\\")\\n    install_sha = install[0]\\n    full_chain = git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", f\\\"{install_sha}..HEAD\\\", \\\"--first-parent\\\").split()\\n    if not full_chain:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no commit after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}; nothing has been recorded\\\")\\n\\n    # issue #74: [doctor] from lets a tenant declare the doctor's read to\\n    # start at a later commit on main's first-parent line -- the point\\n    # after which every push arrived through the queue -- rather than the\\n    # install commit, which on a repository that adopted the product\\n    # after its history began is a boundary the doctor cannot otherwise\\n    # see. Any spelling git resolves is accepted (a short sha, a tag, a\\n    # ref) -- resolved with rev-parse --verify before the first-parent\\n    # check runs, so the two failure modes stay distinct: a spelling that\\n    # names no commit at all, and a commit that names one off the line.\\n    # Checked, not trusted: neither is silently forgiven back to install.\\n    declared_from = (m.get(\\\"doctor\\\") or {}).get(\\\"from\\\")\\n    window_start = install_sha\\n    if declared_from is not None:\\n        try:\\n            resolved_from = git(root, \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", f\\\"{declared_from}^{{commit}}\\\").strip()\\n        except RuntimeError:\\n            return p.fail(f\\\"[doctor] from {declared_from} does not resolve to a commit\\\")\\n        if resolved_from != install_sha and resolved_from not in full_chain:\\n            return p.fail(f\\\"[doctor] from {declared_from} is not on main's first-parent \\\"\\n                          f\\\"line after the install commit {install_sha[:12]}\\\")\\n        window_start = resolved_from\\n\\n    if window_start == install_sha:\\n        window_spec = f\\\"{install_sha}..HEAD\\\"\\n        commits = full_chain\\n    else:\\n        window_spec = f\\\"{window_start}^..HEAD\\\"\\n        commits = git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", window_spec, \\\"--first-parent\\\").split()\\n    before_window = len(full_chain) - len(commits)\\n\\n    records_rel = m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"records\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\\n    named: set[str] = set()\\n    for stages in load_records(records_dir).values():\\n        for rec in stages.values():\\n            sha = rec.get(\\\"sha\\\")\\n            if isinstance(sha, str):\\n                named.add(sha)\\n            for c in rec.get(\\\"commits\\\", []) or []:\\n                if isinstance(c, str):\\n                    named.add(c)\\n    record_commits = set(git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", window_spec, \\\"--first-parent\\\",\\n                             \\\"--\\\", records_rel).split()) if records_rel else set()\\n    merges = set(git(root, \\\"rev-list\\\", window_spec, \\\"--first-parent\\\", \\\"--merges\\\").split())\\n    boundary_paths = ((m.get(\\\"spec\\\") or {}).get(\\\"boundary\\\") or {}).get(\\\"paths\\\") or []\\n\\n    # Every first-parent commit in the window is exactly one of three\\n    # (issue #72): recorded (a record names it, or its diff touches\\n    # paths.records), ordinary (a merge that doesn't), or unrecorded\\n    # (anything else -- on a protected main with a queue, a non-merge\\n    # commit is the only way a change arrives without the forge).\\n    recorded, ordinary, unrecorded = [], [], []\\n    ordinary_commits, unrecorded_commits = [], []\\n    boundary_evasions = 0\\n    for c in commits:\\n        if c in named or c in record_commits:\\n            recorded.append(c)\\n        elif c in merges:\\n            ordinary.append(c)\\n            evasion = bool(boundary_paths and touches_boundary(root, c, boundary_paths))\\n            if evasion:\\n                boundary_evasions += 1\\n            ordinary_commits.append({\\\"sha\\\": c, \\\"subject\\\": commit_subject(root, c),\\n                                     \\\"boundary_evasion\\\": evasion})\\n        else:\\n            unrecorded.append(c)\\n            unrecorded_commits.append({\\\"sha\\\": c, \\\"subject\\\": commit_subject(root, c)})\\n\\n    counts = f\\\"{len(recorded)} recorded, {len(ordinary)} ordinary, {len(unrecorded)} unrecorded\\\"\\n    evasions = boundary_evasions if boundary_paths else \\\"n/a\\\"\\n    extra = {\\\"recorded\\\": len(recorded), \\\"ordinary\\\": len(ordinary),\\n             \\\"unrecorded\\\": len(unrecorded), \\\"boundary_evasions\\\": evasions,\\n             \\\"before_window\\\": before_window,\\n             \\\"ordinary_commits\\\": ordinary_commits, \\\"unrecorded_commits\\\": unrecorded_commits}\\n    if unrecorded:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"{unrecorded[-1][:12]} lacks a record; {counts}; boundary evasions: \\\"\\n                      f\\\"{evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\\\", **extra)\\n    return p.hold(f\\\"{counts}; boundary evasions: {evasions}; before the window: {before_window}\\\",\\n                  **extra)\\n\\n\\nADAPTER_EXIT_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^\\\\[adapter exited \\\\d+\\\\]$\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _log_owes_tool_error(log: str | None) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"True when a log's last non-empty line is exactly an adapter-exit\\n    marker and every line before it parses as JSON -- an adapter's own\\n    event stream, never a tool's own words (issue #94's own specimen,\\n    tenant zero's attest/records/659/verify-01.log: codex's\\n    \\\"thread.started\\\" event, then nothing but \\\"[adapter exited 1]\\\" -- the\\n    tool's real error line dropped before this reached the log, issue\\n    #86's own bug in split_adapter_stdout). A log that is only the exit\\n    marker, nothing before it at all, still owes the same line.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not log:\\n        return False\\n    lines = [l for l in log.splitlines() if l.strip()]\\n    if not lines or not ADAPTER_EXIT_RE.match(lines[-1]):\\n        return False\\n    for l in lines[:-1]:\\n        try:\\n            json.loads(l)\\n        except ValueError:\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root: Path, m: dict | None) -> Proof:\\n    p = Proof(\\\"no-stop-lacks-cause\\\", \\\"no stop lacks its cause\\\")\\n    if m is None:\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no {MANIFEST} at {root}; no records directory is declared\\\")\\n    records_rel = m.get(\\\"paths\\\", {}).get(\\\"records\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    records_dir = root / records_rel\\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\\n        return p.fail(f\\\"no records directory under {records_dir}\\\")\\n\\n    # issue #89's own window lesson, proof three's already: a record\\n    # before record_version 3 has no stop by construction (schema\\n    # versions 1 and 2 predate it) -- counted here, never refused.\\n    older = 0\\n    checked = 0\\n    problems: list[str] = []\\n    for item_dir in sorted(d for d in records_dir.iterdir() if d.is_dir()):\\n        for stage in STOP_STAGES:\\n            for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_dir, stage).items()):\\n                if rec.get(\\\"record_version\\\", 1) < 3:\\n                    older += 1\\n                    continue\\n                if rec.get(\\\"status\\\") == \\\"pass\\\":\\n                    continue\\n                checked += 1\\n                name = f\\\"{stage}-{n:02d}\\\"\\n                stop = rec.get(\\\"stop\\\")\\n                if not stop:\\n                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} carries no stop\\\")\\n                    continue\\n                cls, provenance = stop.get(\\\"class\\\"), stop.get(\\\"provenance\\\")\\n                if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\\n                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \\\"\\n                                    f\\\"no enumerated class\\\")\\n                    continue\\n                if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\\n                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \\\"\\n                                    f\\\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\\\")\\n                    continue\\n                if cls == \\\"unclassed\\\" and not stop.get(\\\"detail\\\"):\\n                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is unclassed with no detail\\\")\\n                    continue\\n                log_path = item_dir / f\\\"{name}.log\\\"\\n                log = log_path.read_text() if log_path.is_file() else None\\n                # Issue #89, rejection test 1's own specimen (tenant\\n                # zero's #659 build-01): a failed build that actually ran\\n                # the gates -- selected_tests is set only once cmd_build\\n                # reaches them -- owes their heading in the log, whatever\\n                # else stop already says.\\n                if (stage == \\\"build\\\" and rec.get(\\\"status\\\") == \\\"failed\\\"\\n                        and rec.get(\\\"selected_tests\\\") is not None\\n                        and \\\"--- attavo gates, iteration\\\" not in (log or \\\"\\\")):\\n                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} failed after the gates ran \\\"\\n                                    f\\\"but its log carries no gates heading\\\")\\n                    continue\\n                if _log_owes_tool_error(log):\\n                    problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name}'s log ends in an adapter \\\"\\n                                    f\\\"exit with nothing before it but event lines; the tool's \\\"\\n                                    f\\\"own error line is owed\\\")\\n\\n        # issue #137: a refused spec-gate record is a stop too, class\\n        # \\\"gate\\\" -- synthesized the same way item_stops and\\n        # cmd_file_stops already read it, since cmd_spec_gate itself\\n        # carries no stop field to check for one. No record_version\\n        # gate here: unlike build/verify's own stop field, gate is never\\n        # persisted, so there is no older shape that predates it.\\n        for n, rec in sorted(parse_attempts(item_dir, \\\"spec\\\").items()):\\n            if rec.get(\\\"status\\\") != \\\"refused\\\":\\n                continue\\n            checked += 1\\n            name = f\\\"spec-{n:02d}\\\"\\n            stop = gate_stop(rec.get(\\\"refusal\\\"))\\n            cls, provenance = stop[\\\"class\\\"], stop[\\\"provenance\\\"]\\n            if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\\n                problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.class {cls!r} names \\\"\\n                                f\\\"no enumerated class\\\")\\n                continue\\n            if provenance not in STOP_PROVENANCES:\\n                problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} stop.provenance \\\"\\n                                f\\\"{provenance!r} names no enumerated provenance\\\")\\n                continue\\n            if not stop.get(\\\"detail\\\"):\\n                problems.append(f\\\"item {item_dir.name} {name} is a gate stop with no cause\\\")\\n\\n    older_note = f\\\"{older} record(s) before stop was recorded\\\"\\n    if problems:\\n        return p.fail(\\\"; \\\".join(problems), older_records=older)\\n    return p.hold(f\\\"{checked} checked ({older_note})\\\" if checked == 0\\n                 else f\\\"{checked} non-pass record(s) carry stop with a cause ({older_note})\\\",\\n                 older_records=older)\\n\\n\\ndef doctor(root: Path) -> list[Proof]:\\n    m = read_manifest(root)\\n    return [proof_every_gate_rejects(root, m),\\n            proof_one_item_every_stage(root, m),\\n            proof_no_commit_lacks_record(root, m),\\n            proof_no_stop_lacks_cause(root, m)]\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_doctor(argv: list[str]) -> int:\\n    as_json = \\\"--json\\\" in argv\\n    args = [a for a in argv if a != \\\"--json\\\"]\\n    root = Path(args[0] if args else \\\".\\\").resolve()\\n    proofs = doctor(root)\\n    if as_json:\\n        print(json.dumps({\\\"root\\\": str(root), \\\"done\\\": all(p.holds for p in proofs),\\n                          \\\"proofs\\\": [p.as_dict() for p in proofs]}, indent=2))\\n    else:\\n        for i, p in enumerate(proofs, 1):\\n            print(f\\\"proof {i} {p.key}: {'HOLDS' if p.holds else 'FAILS'}: {p.reason}\\\")\\n        print(\\\"doctor: done\\\" if all(p.holds for p in proofs)\\n              else f\\\"doctor: not done ({sum(not p.holds for p in proofs)} of \\\"\\n                   f\\\"{len(proofs)} proofs fail)\\\")\\n    return 0 if all(p.holds for p in proofs) else 1\\n\\n\\n# --- the spec contract ---\\n\\ndef parse_spec(spec_md: Path) -> tuple[dict | None, str | None]:\\n    lines = spec_md.read_text().splitlines()\\n    heading_idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\\\"## \\\")]\\n    headings = [lines[i].rstrip() for i in heading_idx]\\n    expected = [\\\"## Problem\\\", \\\"## Claims\\\", \\\"## Criteria\\\"]\\n    if headings != expected:\\n        bad = next((h for h in headings if h not in expected), None)\\n        if bad is None:\\n            missing = [h for h in expected if h not in headings]\\n            bad = missing[0] if missing else \\\"heading order\\\"\\n        return None, f\\\"headings: found {headings or ['(none)']}, expected {expected} ({bad})\\\"\\n    idx_problem, idx_claims, idx_criteria = heading_idx\\n    claims = [l.strip()[2:].strip() for l in lines[idx_claims + 1:idx_criteria]\\n              if l.strip().startswith(\\\"- \\\")]\\n    criteria = []\\n    for l in lines[idx_criteria + 1:]:\\n        s = l.strip()\\n        if not s.startswith(\\\"- \\\") or \\\":\\\" not in s:\\n            continue\\n        name = s[2:].split(\\\":\\\", 1)[0].strip()\\n        criteria.append(name)\\n    return {\\\"claims\\\": claims, \\\"criteria\\\": criteria}, None\\n\\n\\ndef run_criterion(exe: Path, cwd: Path) -> int:\\n    try:\\n        run = subprocess.run([str(exe)], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True,\\n                             timeout=CRITERION_TIMEOUT, check=False)\\n        return run.returncode\\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\\n        return 124\\n    except OSError:\\n        return 126\\n\\n\\ndef parse_removed(stub_dir: Path) -> list[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The paths listed in stub/.removed, one per line, comments (lines\\n    starting with #) and blank lines ignored. [] when the stub carries no\\n    .removed at all.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    removed_file = stub_dir / \\\".removed\\\"\\n    if not removed_file.is_file():\\n        return []\\n    paths = []\\n    for line in removed_file.read_text().splitlines():\\n        s = line.strip()\\n        if not s or s.startswith(\\\"#\\\"):\\n            continue\\n        paths.append(s)\\n    return paths\\n\\n\\ndef removed_path_refusal(root: Path, stub_dir: Path, rel: str) -> str | None:\\n    p = Path(rel)\\n    if p.is_absolute() or \\\"..\\\" in p.parts:\\n        return f\\\"stub/.removed names a path outside the tree: {rel}\\\"\\n    if not (root / p).exists():\\n        return f\\\"stub/.removed names a path not in the tree: {rel}\\\"\\n    if (stub_dir / p).exists():\\n        return f\\\"stub/.removed names a path the stub also supplies: {rel}\\\"\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef stub_removed_refusal(root: Path, spec_dir: Path) -> str | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validated by name, before any criterion runs -- a stub whose\\n    .removed cannot be applied has no meaning to gate against.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    stub_dir = spec_dir / \\\"stub\\\"\\n    for rel in parse_removed(stub_dir):\\n        refusal = removed_path_refusal(root, stub_dir, rel)\\n        if refusal:\\n            return refusal\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef run_criteria(root: Path, spec_dir: Path, names: list[str]) -> list[dict]:\\n    criteria_dir = spec_dir / \\\"criteria\\\"\\n    stub_dir = spec_dir / \\\"stub\\\"\\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\\n        tree = Path(tmp) / \\\"tree\\\"\\n        stubbed = Path(tmp) / \\\"stubbed\\\"\\n        shutil.copytree(root, tree, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(\\\".git\\\"))\\n        shutil.copytree(root, stubbed, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(\\\".git\\\"))\\n        if stub_dir.is_dir():\\n            shutil.copytree(stub_dir, stubbed, dirs_exist_ok=True)\\n            for rel in parse_removed(stub_dir):\\n                target = stubbed / rel\\n                if target.is_dir():\\n                    shutil.rmtree(target)\\n                elif target.exists():\\n                    target.unlink()\\n            removed_marker = stubbed / \\\".removed\\\"\\n            if removed_marker.exists():\\n                removed_marker.unlink()\\n        results = []\\n        for name in names:\\n            exe = criteria_dir / name\\n            results.append({\\\"name\\\": name,\\n                            \\\"on_tree\\\": run_criterion(exe, tree),\\n                            \\\"on_stub\\\": run_criterion(exe, stubbed)})\\n        return results\\n\\n\\ndef commit_postdates(root: Path, earlier: str, later: str) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Whether later is a strict descendant of earlier on this branch.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if earlier == later:\\n        return False\\n    run = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"merge-base\\\", \\\"--is-ancestor\\\", earlier, later],\\n                         capture_output=True, check=False)\\n    return run.returncode == 0\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_spec_gate(argv: list[str]) -> int:\\n    root = Path(\\\".\\\").resolve()\\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\\n    if not item_id:\\n        print(\\\"attavo spec-gate: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\\\",\\n              file=sys.stderr)\\n        return 2\\n    m = read_manifest(root)\\n    if m is None:\\n        print(f\\\"attavo spec-gate: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        return 2\\n    specs_rel = m[\\\"paths\\\"][\\\"specs\\\"]\\n    records_rel = m[\\\"paths\\\"][\\\"records\\\"]\\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\\n    spec_md = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n    if not spec_md.is_file():\\n        print(f\\\"attavo spec-gate: no spec at {spec_dir}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        return 2\\n    spec_rel = str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id)\\n    try:\\n        spec_sha = last_commit_touching(root, spec_rel)\\n    except ShallowCheckoutError as exc:\\n        print(f\\\"attavo spec-gate: refused: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        return 2\\n\\n    records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\\n    try:\\n        approved = approval_status(root, m, item_id) == \\\"valid\\\"\",\"numLines\":1243,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":3393,\"truncatedByTokenCap\":true}}}\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d\",\"uuid\":\"d43c7c86-27b9-46df-a4cf-9caca1694e5d\"}\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":105,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":55,\"session_id\":\"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d\",\"uuid\":\"b24d2768-b48f-4169-b6ed-18f6eb061b02\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cf9abbtAy5Fnj5LXMN6HP\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":25085,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":33941,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":25085},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f081a203-e2ee-47b3-8bf8-5fc3aaeb804d\",\"uuid\":\"e1fdf6f8-3145-4601-8759-dedb9ff22f20\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-17T19:40:47.408Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cf9abbPep7nP3xGZYkaRZ\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cf9abbtAy5Fnj5LXMN6HP\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_017jmo58HBYu9ZtEm6nYBN69\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"died\\\\|hung\\\\|stall_after_s\\\\|--recover\\\\|\\\\.started\\\\|no-invocation-lacks-record\\\\|recover\\\" bin/attavo\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":25085,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":33941,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":25085},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f081a203-e2ee-4